--[[
	Anomaly Coop - shared tasks in Lua (gamedata\scripts\coop_tasks.script), work package W3c.
	SPEC R-7.2, R-7.5, R-7.6, R-7.8. Engine side: src\xrGame\coop\coop_story.cpp (WP4 + W3c).

	One task manager for the whole group: the HOST's Anomaly task_manager. The engine layer (coop_story)
	already mirrors the engine task list (texts, targets, states, PDA spots) to every client. This script
	does the same for the Lua side and routes every task decision to the host:

	Client (connected, in the host's world):
	  - task_manager:give_task / set_task_completed / set_task_failed / set_task_cancelled are sent to the
	    host (event coop_tq) and are NOT run locally, so on-give effects, on_complete, rewards and news run
	    exactly once, on the host (R-7.8, item 4 of W3c). The task vars a dialog prepared in this player's
	    pstor (fetch item, stash target, keys starting with the task id) travel with the give request.
	  - The client never evaluates tasks (no status functors, no completion checks): its task_manager holds
	    stubs mirrored from the host (stage, status, giver, task vars), so dialogs that read
	    task_info[id].stage / .status / .task_giver_id offer the same turn-in and cancel options as on the
	    host, for every task, including tasks the host gave after this client joined (R-7.2).
	    A dialog script that writes stub.stage or stub.forced_status sends that to the host as well.
	Host:
	  - Runs the requests with Anomaly's own task_manager and remembers who took and who turned in a task.
	    In the task callback the rewards go to the player who turned it in (R-7.6): money through the host
	    ledger (coop.money_grant onto the player's character, F2 T6; the client only gets the news line in
	    event coop_trw), items spawned by the host into that player's character, goodwill/faction effects
	    keyed to that character. Console coop_share_rewards: 1 splits money equally among the online players,
	    2 and 3 reward everyone who played, split or in full (coop_reward_group.script);
	    items still go to the finisher.
	  - Quest items count from any group member's inventory (R-7.5): fetch / stash status functors also count
	    the other players' characters, and removing the items takes them from whoever holds them (the player
	    who turned the task in first).
	  - Broadcasts the Lua task state (coop_tl, on change, scanned every 0.5 s), a digest list every 10 s
	    (coop_tl_list, in parts of 200 tasks) and the full state on request (coop_tl_req).
	  - Group task bookkeeping in the actor's pstor (keys "drx_sl_*": givers with outstanding tasks, the
	    current storyline task, ...) is the host's: mirrored to clients (coop_tv: the keys that changed, the whole set in
	    parts for a sync, never an empty set for a set that got long); a client's save_var of such a key goes to the host
	    (coop_tvd, giver counters as deltas, the rest as values), so a giver's "has a task for you" state is the same for
	    everybody.
	  - What a task's end does to the character of the player who turned it in (statistics, rank, reputation, faction)
	    runs on that player's machine (coop_trw k = stat, fx), whatever coop_share_rewards says. His machine answers
	    (coop_trw_ok); unanswered effects go out again on his next coop_tl_req.
	  - While the host's actor is dead the stock binder stops before task_manager:update and the actor_on_update callback:
	    a frame call (level.add_call) goes on with both, so the group's tasks do not stand still.
	  - Messages (docs\MESSAGES.md): the host's news_manager.send_task ("new" / "updated" / "complete" / "fail" / "reversed")
	    goes to every client as event coop_tn with the player who caused it. A client shows the stock line for its own
	    action and for an event nobody caused, "<nick> took / completed / failed / cancelled a task" (coop_quests_news)
	    for another player's; the host does the same for a client's action. The client's own send_task for a group
	    task is swallowed: the engine fires the actor's task callback for the copy it applies ("new"), a second line.
	API for scripts (any machine):
	  coop_tasks.party_has(section, count, min_condition) -> bool   (also coop.party_has when not set)
	  coop_tasks.party_count(section, min_condition)      -> number (multi-use items count their uses)
	    Host: the host's actor + the characters of all connected players. Client: own actor + the other
	    players' characters as mirrored here.
	  coop_tasks.party_object(section) -> item of that section held by another player's character, or nil
	  coop_tasks.party_holds_id(item_id, section) -> true if a player character holds that item
	  coop_tasks.recipient(task_id) -> peer that would get the reward now (host only)
	  coop_tasks.taker(task_id) -> peer that took the task (host only; 0 = the host)
	  coop_tasks.reward_peer() -> client peer that gets the effects being run now, or nil (host only)
	  coop_tasks.active_of(peer) -> the task that player has as his active one (host only, nil: none reported)
	  coop_tasks.run_as(peer, fn, ...) -> runs fn as a request of that player (host: gives / turn-ins
	    inside belong to that player)
	  coop_tasks.with_task_owner(task_id, fn, ...) -> runs fn with the companions it adds and the effects keyed to the actor going
	    to the player who took the task (host: items a status functor hands out, news)
	  coop_tasks.with_recipient(peer, fn, ...) -> the same for a given player (host)
	  coop_tasks.in_reward_scope() -> true while such effects belong to one player (host)
	  coop_tasks.party_take(section, amount) -> removes that many items from the group (host), count
	  coop_tasks.party_inventory_walker(real) -> an iterate_inventory over every player's character (host, for one call)
	  coop_tasks.taker_money(task_id) -> the ledger balance of the client who took the task (host; nil: the host took it)
	  coop_tasks.giving_npc() -> the giver of the client's give request being run (host; nil outside one)
	  coop_tasks.give_to_peer(peer, money, sections) -> money / items for one player (host)
	  coop_tasks.news_actor(kind, task_id) -> peer, cancelled: the player whose action caused a task event ("new" |
	    "complete" | "fail"; 0 = the host, nil = nobody: a script, a timer). The one rule the task lines and any
	    other report of "who did it" (docs\MESSAGES.md, docs\ABSENT_REWARDS.md) share. Host only.
	  coop_tasks.money_line(peer, n) -> the "money received" line on that player's machine for money the host
	    changed outside a task reward (the achievement money of coop_quests_pda). Host only.
	  coop_tasks.set_local_task(task_id) -> a personal task (xrRazom xrr_local_tasks): given, checked
	    and finished on the machine that has it, never sent to the host or mirrored
	Called by the engine: coop_tasks.host_note(task_id, "taker"|"finisher", peer)  (coop_story.cpp requests)
--]]

local api = rawget(_G, "coop") -- engine namespace (nil on an exe without co-op)

local tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next = tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next
local string_format, string_char, table_concat, table_sort = string.format, string.char, table.concat, table.sort
local math_floor, math_max = math.floor, math.max

local EV_REQ = "coop_tq" -- client -> host: task operation
local EV_STATE = "coop_tl" -- host -> client(s): Lua state of one task
local EV_LIST = "coop_tl_list" -- host -> client(s): ids + digests of all tasks
local EV_SYNC = "coop_tl_req" -- client -> host: send me everything
local EV_REWARD = "coop_trw" -- host -> one client: money / news / personal effect for this player
local EV_NEWS = "coop_tn" -- host -> clients: a task line (new / updated / complete / fail / reversed) and who caused it
local EV_VARS = "coop_tv" -- host -> client(s): the group's shared task bookkeeping vars (whole set)
local EV_VAR = "coop_tvd" -- client -> host: this client's dialog changed one of them
local EV_ACK = "coop_trw_ok" -- client -> host: the effect of a coop_trw event ran here

-- Actor pstor keys that are task bookkeeping of the whole group (DRX storyline: givers with outstanding
-- tasks, current storyline task, ...). Written by the giving dialog on whichever machine, read by dialog
-- preconditions everywhere, cleared by on_complete on the host. Host-owned, mirrored, client writes routed.
-- Later ones: the escort tasks' target anomaly, its level and analyzed flag | Warfare escort's target smart (read by the
-- companion tasks' "arrived" test) | the counters of the Zaton b33 and Jupiter b200 dialog quests (several players count them)
local SHARED_PREFIXES = { "drx_sl_", "task_target_anomaly", "warfare_escort_", "zat_b33_", "jup_b200_" }
local COUNTER_PREFIX = "drx_sl_task_giver_" -- the only numbers that several players count at once: these travel as deltas

local SCAN_MS = 500
local LIST_MS = 10000
local SYNC_RETRY_MS = 10000
local PENDING_MS = 15000 -- provisional give / optimistic turn-in without an answer from the host
local MAX_STATE = 12000 -- characters of one state message (event payload limit is 16 KiB)
local LIST_IDS = 200 -- tasks in one part of the digest list
local DEAD_UPDATE_MS = 500 -- task_manager:update while the actor is dead (the stock binder: every frame)

local CONTAINERS = { "lead_box", "af_aam", "af_aac", "af_iam" } -- artefact containers (stock suffixes)
local FETCH_MIN_COND = { -- stock actor_has_fetch_item asks for a minimal condition on these two
	esc_2_12_stalker_nimble_task_1 = 0.9,
	jup_b220_trapper_task_3 = 0.9,
}
-- Effects that change the turning-in player's own character: run on that player's machine (R-3.4).
local FORWARD_EFFECTS = { drx_sl_change_factions = true }
-- game_statistics counters of a task's end. With rank and reputation they are the character's of the player who turned
-- the task in, for every coop_share_rewards.
local TASK_STATS = { tasks_completed = true, tasks_failed = true, tasks_cancelled = true }
local MONEY_FUNCTOR = "drx_sl_money_task_status" -- DRX money tasks (faction change): the finisher pays from his own money
local WAIT_FUNCTOR = "check_if_enough_time_passed" -- tm_yantar: Sakharov's helmet upgrade, a wait counted from the give

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Logging, roles
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function log(fmt, ...)
	local ok, line = pcall(string_format, fmt, ...)
	printf("[coop-tasks] %s", ok and line or tostring(fmt))
end

local stats = {
	req_out = 0, req_in = 0, refused = 0, state_out = 0, state_in = 0, lists = 0, syncs = 0,
	rewards_routed = 0, rewards_in = 0, party_moves = 0, party_releases = 0, stage_by_party = 0, errors = 0,
	news_out = 0, news_in = 0, news_swallowed = 0, news_limited = 0,
}

local function report(what, err)
	stats.errors = stats.errors + 1
	if stats.errors <= 10 or stats.errors % 100 == 0 then
		log("! %s: %s", tostring(what), tostring(err))
	end
end

local function active()
	if not api then return false end
	local ok, v = pcall(api.is_active)
	return ok and v == true
end
local function is_host() return active() and api.is_host() == true end
local function is_client() return active() and api.is_client() == true end
-- A task of the stock manager is a luabind object, type() says "userdata"; a client's mirror stub is a Lua table.
function is_task(t)
	local kind = type(t)
	return kind == "userdata" or kind == "table"
end
local function client_live() return is_client() and api.is_live() == true end

local function self_peer()
	local ok, v = pcall(api.self_id)
	return ok and tonumber(v) or 0
end

local function players()
	if not api then return {} end
	local ok, list = pcall(api.players)
	return ok and type(list) == "table" and list or {}
end

local function to_host_id(id)
	if not (api and api.to_host_id and type(id) == "number") then return id end
	return api.to_host_id(id) or id
end
local function to_local_id(id)
	if not (api and api.to_local_id and type(id) == "number") then return id end
	return api.to_local_id(id) or id
end

local function tmgr()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	if not (mod and mod.get_task_manager) then return nil end
	local ok, tm = pcall(mod.get_task_manager)
	return ok and tm or nil
end

local function now() return time_global() end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Payloads: "k=v;k=v" of scalars, values may be one level of flat table ("t" + "k:v,k:v").
-- No code is ever loaded from the network.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function esc(s)
	return (tostring(s):gsub("[%%;=,:]", function(c) return string_format("%%%02X", c:byte()) end))
end
local function unesc(s)
	return (s:gsub("%%(%x%x)", function(h) return string_char(tonumber(h, 16)) end))
end

local function enc_scalar(v)
	local tv = type(v)
	if tv == "number" then
		if v ~= v or v == math.huge or v == -math.huge then return nil end
		return "n" .. string_format("%.17g", v)
	elseif tv == "boolean" then
		return v and "b1" or "b0"
	elseif tv == "string" then
		return "s" .. v
	end
	return nil
end

local function dec_scalar(v)
	local tag, body = v:sub(1, 1), v:sub(2)
	if tag == "n" then return tonumber(body) end
	if tag == "b" then return body == "1" end
	if tag == "s" then return body end
	return nil
end

-- flat table of scalars -> "k:v,..." (keys typed: "$" string, "#" number); nil if it holds anything else
local function enc_flat(t)
	local out = {}
	for k, v in pairs(t) do
		local ek
		if type(k) == "string" then
			ek = "$" .. k
		elseif type(k) == "number" then
			ek = "#" .. string_format("%.17g", k)
		end
		local ev = enc_scalar(v)
		if not (ek and ev) then return nil end
		out[#out + 1] = esc(ek) .. ":" .. esc(ev)
	end
	table_sort(out)
	return table_concat(out, ",")
end

local function dec_flat(s)
	local t = {}
	for pair in s:gmatch("[^,]+") do
		local k, v = pair:match("^([^:]*):(.*)$")
		if k then
			k = unesc(k)
			local tag, body = k:sub(1, 1), k:sub(2)
			local key = (tag == "#" and tonumber(body)) or (tag == "$" and body) or nil
			local val = dec_scalar(unesc(v))
			if key ~= nil and val ~= nil then t[key] = val end
		end
	end
	return t
end

local function pack(t, allow_tables)
	local out = {}
	for k, v in pairs(t) do
		if type(k) == "string" then
			local ev
			if type(v) == "table" then
				if allow_tables then
					local f = enc_flat(v)
					ev = f and ("t" .. f) or nil
				end
			else
				ev = enc_scalar(v)
			end
			if ev then out[#out + 1] = esc(k) .. "=" .. esc(ev) end
		end
	end
	table_sort(out)
	return table_concat(out, ";")
end

local function unpack_payload(s)
	local t = {}
	if type(s) ~= "string" then return t end
	for pair in s:gmatch("[^;]+") do
		local k, v = pair:match("^([^=]*)=(.*)$")
		if k then
			k, v = unesc(k), unesc(v)
			if v:sub(1, 1) == "t" then
				t[k] = dec_flat(v:sub(2))
			else
				local val = dec_scalar(v)
				if val ~= nil then t[k] = val end
			end
		end
	end
	return t
end

local function digest(s)
	local h = 5381
	for i = 1, #s do h = (h * 33 + s:byte(i)) % 4294967296 end
	return string_format("%08x", h)
end

-- Task vars a dialog or a task script keeps in the actor's pstor: keys that start with the task id
-- (fetch item "<id>_fetch", counts, stash/delivery tables saved under "<id>").
local function var_value_ok(v)
	local tv = type(v)
	if tv == "number" or tv == "string" or tv == "boolean" then return true end
	return tv == "table" and enc_flat(v) ~= nil
end

local function actor_pstor(create)
	local actor = db and db.actor
	local st = actor and db.storage and db.storage[actor:id()]
	if not st then return nil end
	if not st.pstor and create then st.pstor = {} end
	return st.pstor
end

-- The task's own vars: the key is the task id or starts with "<id>_" (not "<id>0", another task's).
local function is_task_key(k, id)
	if type(k) ~= "string" then return false end
	local n = #id
	if k:sub(1, n) ~= id then return false end
	return #k == n or k:sub(n + 1, n + 1) == "_"
end

local function task_vars(id)
	local out = {}
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	if not ps then return out end
	for k, v in pairs(ps) do
		if is_task_key(k, id) and var_value_ok(v) then out[k] = v end
	end
	return out
end

-- Personal tasks (xrRazom xrr_local_tasks): never routed to the host, never mirrored.
local local_tasks = {}
local function is_local(id) return type(id) == "string" and local_tasks[id] == true end

-- Needs the engine side too: coop_story must give/finish the engine task of such an id locally as well.
-- Without coop.story_local_task the request is refused (the engine would still send the task to the host).
function set_local_task(id)
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" then return false end
	if not (api and api.story_local_task) then
		log("! personal task '%s' not set: the engine has no coop.story_local_task", id)
		return false
	end
	-- true = the engine keeps it local; false = refused (id over 256 chars, more than 1024 tasks)
	local ok, res = pcall(api.story_local_task, id)
	if ok and res then
		local_tasks[id] = true
		return true
	end
	log("! personal task '%s' refused by the engine (%s)", id, ok and "limit" or tostring(res))
	return false
end

function is_local_task(id) return is_local(id) end

-- Bounty targets are chosen while the dialog builds its text (setup_bounty_task) and kept in
-- axr_task_manager.bounties_by_id, not in the pstor: they travel with the task too.
local function bounties()
	local atm = rawget(_G, "axr_task_manager") or axr_task_manager
	local t = atm and atm.bounties_by_id
	return type(t) == "table" and t or nil
end

local function is_shared_key(k)
	if type(k) ~= "string" then return false end
	for _, p in ipairs(SHARED_PREFIXES) do
		if k:sub(1, #p) == p then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Group inventories (R-7.5)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A player on another level, as coop_quests_core answers for him. Not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit (test_engine_header).
function far_of(peer, id)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core") or coop_quests_core
	return qc and qc.far_body and qc.far_body(peer, id) or nil
end

-- Characters of the group on this machine: own actor first, then the other connected players, those on another level as far_body.
local function party()
	local out = {}
	-- the actor of a dedicated host or of a map server is nobody's character (owner 2026-11-13)
	local ghost = api and ((api.is_dedicated and api.is_dedicated()) or (api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server()))
	if db and db.actor and not ghost then out[1] = { obj = db.actor, peer = self_peer(), self = true } end
	if not active() then return out end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self and p.avatar_id then
			local o = level.object_by_id(p.avatar_id) or far_of(p.id, p.avatar_id)
			if o then out[#out + 1] = { obj = o, peer = p.id } end
		end
	end
	return out
end

local function uses_of(sec)
	return IsItem and IsItem("multiuse", sec) or nil
end

-- Units of `sec` in one inventory (multi-use items count their uses, like utils_item.get_amount mode 1).
local function count_in(obj, sec, min_cond)
	local n = 0
	local multi = uses_of(sec)
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if item:section() == sec and (not min_cond or (item:condition() or 1) >= min_cond) then
				n = n + (multi and item:get_remaining_uses() or 1)
			end
		end, nil)
	end)
	if not ok then report("count " .. tostring(sec), err) end
	return n
end

function party_count(section, min_cond)
	if type(section) ~= "string" or section == "" then return 0 end
	local n = 0
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do n = n + count_in(h.obj, section, min_cond) end
	return n
end

function party_has(section, count, min_cond)
	return party_count(section, min_cond) >= (tonumber(count) or 1)
end

-- An item of `section` in another player's character on this machine (not the own actor), or nil.
function party_object(section)
	if type(section) ~= "string" or not active() then return nil end
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if not h.self then
			local ok, o = pcall(h.obj.object, h.obj, section)
			if ok and o then return o end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- True if the item `item_id` (of `section`, if given) is held by a player character on this machine.
function party_holds_id(item_id, section)
	if type(item_id) ~= "number" then return false end
	local o = level.object_by_id(item_id)
	local pid
	if o then
		if section and o:section() ~= section then return false end
		local ok, p = pcall(o.parent, o)
		if not (ok and p) then return false end
		pid = p:id()
	else -- on another level: the record says who has it
		local se = alife_object(item_id)
		if not se or (section and se:section_name() ~= section) then return false end
		pid = se.parent_id
	end
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if h.obj:id() == pid then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host state
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local host = {
	sent = {}, -- id -> last broadcast state string
	taker = {}, -- id -> peer that took the task (0 = host)
	finisher = {}, -- id -> peer that turned it in / cancelled it, until the task callback uses it
	taker_note = {}, -- id -> peer told by the engine (coop_story) right before the give
	given_by = {}, -- id -> peer whose action gave the task (0 = the host's dialog); nil: a script gave it (news only)
	news_seen = {}, -- "<kind> <id>" -> time of the last tn event sent (dedupe)
	news_count = 0,
	exec_peer = nil, -- peer whose request is being executed
	giver = nil, -- giver (npc id) of the client's give request being run
	next_scan = 0,
	next_list = 0,
	shared = {}, -- key -> encoded "k=v" pair of a shared var as the clients have it
	shared_long = {}, -- key -> true: its value does not fit a message, the clients keep what they have
	shared_gen = 0, -- number of the last full set
	list_gen = 0, -- number of the last digest list
	active = {}, -- peer -> the task that client has as his active one
	fx_seq = 0,
	fx_wait = {}, -- effect_key(peer) -> { { q, s }, ... } effects his machine has not answered yet
	char_of = {}, -- peer -> his character (it outlives the peer: a player who left, a reconnect)
	taker_char = {}, -- task -> persistent character; a reconnect can reuse the peer slot
	participants = {}, -- task -> character ids captured when the task is accepted
	rep_party = {}, -- task -> character ids in game at the accept, always (the session rule rep_share)
	failure_participants = {}, -- a missed deadline is a group consequence even with individual item rewards
	map_seen = {},
	fines = {}, -- character -> pending guide fine; never a reusable peer slot
	map_epoch = tostring(os.time()) .. ":" .. tostring(time_global()) .. ":" .. tostring({}),
	map_retry = 0,
	give_near = nil, -- object of the condlist effect that is giving a task
	next_dead_update = 0,
}
local ctx = nil -- host: { task, rcpt (peer), share, owner } while a task callback hands out rewards
local raw_create = nil -- alife_create_item without the reward redirect

function reward_group()
	return _G.coop_reward_group
end

function news_mod() return _G.coop_quests_news end

-- Host: the setting coop_share_rewards. 0 the finisher, 1 money split online, 2 and 3 see coop_reward_group.script.
local EVERYONE_SHARED, EVERYONE_FULL = 2, 3

local function reward_mode()
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return get_console():get_integer("coop_share_rewards") end)
	return ok and tonumber(v) or 0
end

-- Host: the session rule rep_share (docs\GAME_SETTINGS.md). "everyone" (default): the personal effects of a completed
-- task (statistics, reputation, faction goodwill) go in full to every character in game at the accept or at the end;
-- "taker": only to the player who took / turned it in. Money and items stay with coop_share_rewards.
function rep_share_rule() -- not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit of 200 locals
	local ok, v = pcall(function()
		local core = _G.coop_economy_core
		return core and core.rule and core.rule("rep_share")
	end)
	return ok and v == "taker" and "taker" or "everyone"
end

-- Host: character of a peer (0 = the host's actor), the far_body of one on another level; nil: he left the game.
local function avatar_obj(peer)
	if peer == nil then return nil end
	if peer == 0 or peer == self_peer() then return db.actor end
	local ok, id = pcall(api.avatar_of, peer)
	return ok and id and (level.object_by_id(id) or far_of(peer, id)) or nil
end

function character_of(peer)
	if ctx and ctx.rcpt == peer and ctx.character ~= nil then return ctx.character end
	if peer == 0 then return 0 end
	local rg = reward_group()
	local id = rg and rg.id_of(peer)
	if id == nil and api.avatar_of then id = api.avatar_of(peer) end
	if id ~= nil then host.char_of[peer] = id end
	return id or host.char_of[peer]
end

function peer_for_character(id)
	if id == 0 then return 0 end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do if p.avatar_id == id then return p.id end end
	local rg = reward_group()
	for _, m in ipairs(rg and rg.list() or {}) do if m.id == id then return m.peer end end
end

function recipient_body(peer)
	local id = character_of(peer)
	if id == 0 then
		local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
		return p and p.own_actor and p.own_actor() or db.actor
	end
	if id == nil then return nil end
	local o = level.object_by_id(id)
	if o then return o end
	local qc = _G.coop_quests_core
	return qc and qc.body_for_character and qc.body_for_character(id)
end

function participant_ids()
	local ids, seen = {}, {}
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		local id = p.is_self and self_peer() == 0 and 0 or p.avatar_id
		if id ~= nil and not seen[id] then ids[#ids + 1], seen[id] = id, true end
	end
	return ids
end

function peer_in_session(peer) -- not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit of 200 with the engine's two (test_engine_header)
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == peer then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function has_clients()
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function send(name, payload, target)
	local ok, sent = pcall(api.send_event, name, payload, target)
	return ok and sent == true
end

-- One walk of the pstor for a whole scan: the vars of every task of `info` (task id -> table of vars, see is_task_key; an id
-- may hold "_" itself, so every cut at a "_" is looked up) and the group's shared vars. With thousands of keys and dozens of
-- tasks a walk per task every 0.5 s is hundreds of thousands of string operations a second on the host.
local function scan_vars(info)
	local by_task, shared = {}, {}
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	if not ps then return by_task, shared end
	local function add(id, k, v)
		local t = by_task[id]
		if not t then
			t = {}
			by_task[id] = t
		end
		t[k] = v
	end
	for k, v in pairs(ps) do
		if type(k) == "string" and var_value_ok(v) then
			if is_shared_key(k) then shared[k] = v end
			if info[k] ~= nil then add(k, k, v) end
			local at = k:find("_", 2, true)
			while at do
				local id = k:sub(1, at - 1)
				if info[id] ~= nil then add(id, k, v) end
				at = k:find("_", at + 1, true)
			end
		end
	end
	return by_task, shared
end

local function task_record(id, tsk, vars)
	local rec = { i = id }
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		if type(tsk.stage) == "number" then rec.st = tsk.stage end
		if type(tsk.status) == "string" then rec.s = tsk.status end
		if type(tsk.task_giver_id) == "number" then rec.g = tsk.task_giver_id end
	end)
	if not ok then report("task state " .. id, err) end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(b[id]) == "number" then rec.bt = b[id] end
	local v = pack(vars or task_vars(id), true)
	if v ~= "" then rec.v = v end
	local s = pack(rec)
	if #s > MAX_STATE then
		rec.v, rec.nv = nil, true -- too many vars: the state still goes out, the client keeps the vars it has
		s = pack(rec)
	end
	return s
end

-- Groups of entries { s = encoded pair } whose pairs fit one message each.
local function pair_groups(entries)
	table_sort(entries, function(a, b) return a.s < b.s end)
	local groups, cur, size = {}, {}, 0
	for _, e in ipairs(entries) do
		if size + #e.s + 1 > MAX_STATE and #cur > 0 then
			groups[#groups + 1] = cur
			cur, size = {}, 0
		end
		cur[#cur + 1] = e
		size = size + #e.s + 1
	end
	if #cur > 0 then groups[#groups + 1] = cur end
	return groups
end

local function group_text(group)
	local out = {}
	for i, e in ipairs(group) do out[i] = e.s end
	return table_concat(out, ";")
end

-- One value of a shared var, as a pair; nil and a log line if it does not fit a message (the clients keep what they have).
local function shared_pair(k, v)
	local s = pack({ [k] = v }, true)
	if #s <= MAX_STATE then
		host.shared_long[k] = nil
		return s
	end
	if not host.shared_long[k] then log("! shared task var '%s' too long (%d characters), not mirrored", k, #s) end
	host.shared_long[k] = true
	return nil
end

-- The keys that changed since the last scan go to every client ("-key" = removed). An unsent group is sent again by the
-- next scan: host.shared moves only with what went out.
local function host_shared_delta(vars)
	local entries = {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		local s = shared_pair(k, v)
		if s and host.shared[k] ~= s then entries[#entries + 1] = { k = k, s = s, v = s } end
	end
	for k in pairs(host.shared) do
		if vars[k] == nil then entries[#entries + 1] = { k = k, s = pack({ ["-" .. k] = true }) } end
	end
	for k in pairs(host.shared_long) do
		if vars[k] == nil then host.shared_long[k] = nil end
	end
	if #entries == 0 then return end
	for _, group in ipairs(pair_groups(entries)) do
		if send(EV_VARS, group_text(group), -1) then
			for _, e in ipairs(group) do host.shared[e.k] = e.v end
		end
	end
end

-- The whole set to one player, in parts. His keys that are not in it go with the last part, if every part came.
local function host_shared_full(peer)
	local entries = {}
	local _, vars = scan_vars({})
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		entries[#entries + 1] = { s = shared_pair(k, v) or pack({ ["+" .. k] = true }) } -- "+key": it stays as it is there
	end
	local groups = pair_groups(entries)
	if #groups == 0 then groups[1] = {} end
	host.shared_gen = host.shared_gen + 1
	for i, group in ipairs(groups) do
		local head = pack({ _f = host.shared_gen, _p = i, _n = #groups })
		send(EV_VARS, #group > 0 and (head .. ";" .. group_text(group)) or head, peer)
	end
end

local function host_scan(force)
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local by_task, shared = scan_vars(tm.task_info)
	local seen = {}
	for id, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		if type(id) == "string" and not is_local(id) then
			seen[id] = true
			local s = task_record(id, tsk, by_task[id] or {})
			if force or host.sent[id] ~= s then
				host.sent[id] = s
				send(EV_STATE, s, -1)
				stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
			end
		end
	end
	for id in pairs(host.sent) do
		if not seen[id] then
			host.sent[id] = nil
			send(EV_STATE, pack({ i = id, d = true }), -1)
			stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
		end
	end
	host_shared_delta(shared)
end

-- The digest list in parts: "<list>/<part>/<parts>|id:digest,id:digest...". A client acts on a list that came whole.
local function host_list(target)
	local list = {}
	for id, s in pairs(host.sent) do list[#list + 1] = esc(id) .. ":" .. digest(s) end
	table_sort(list)
	local parts = math_max(1, math.ceil(#list / LIST_IDS))
	host.list_gen = host.list_gen + 1
	for i = 1, parts do
		local items = {}
		for j = (i - 1) * LIST_IDS + 1, math.min(i * LIST_IDS, #list) do items[#items + 1] = list[j] end
		send(EV_LIST, string_format("%d/%d/%d|%s", host.list_gen, i, parts, table_concat(items, ",")), target)
	end
	stats.lists = stats.lists + 1
end

-- The current state of one task (or its removal) to one player.
local function host_send_state(id, peer)
	local tm = tmgr()
	local tsk = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
	local s = tsk ~= nil and task_record(id, tsk) or pack({ i = id, d = true })
	send(EV_STATE, s, peer)
	stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
end

local function host_full_sync(peer)
	host_scan(false) -- everybody gets pending changes first, so host.sent is current
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm then return end
	for id in pairs(host.sent) do
		send(EV_STATE, host.sent[id], peer)
		stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
	end
	host_shared_full(peer)
	host_list(peer)
	stats.syncs = stats.syncs + 1
end

-- A client's dialog changed a shared bookkeeping var: counters as a delta (several players may count
-- at once), anything else as the new value.
local function host_on_var(payload, from)
	if not is_host() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local k = t.k
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not (is_shared_key(k) and ps) then return end
	if t.op == "add" and type(t.d) == "number" then
		ps[k] = (tonumber(ps[k]) or 0) + t.d
	elseif t.op == "set" and t.v ~= nil and var_value_ok(t.v) then
		ps[k] = t.v
	elseif t.op == "del" then
		ps[k] = nil
	else
		return
	end
	host_scan(false)
end

-- Who gets the reward of `id` now: the player who turned it in, else who took it, else the host.
function recipient(id)
	local r = host.finisher[id]
	if r == nil then r = host.taker[id] end
	return r or 0
end

function taker(id)
	return host.taker[id] or 0
end

-- The player who took task `id` is in the session and not in the world (on his loading screen): true. One who left is not waited for.
function taker_away(id)
	local t = host.taker[id]
	if not t or t == 0 then return false end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == t then return p.avatar_id == nil end
	end
	return false
end

-- Host: the giver of the task a client's request is giving right now (the speaker an on_init effect asks the
-- host's dialog for; the host is not talking then), or nil.
function giving_npc()
	local id = host.giver
	return type(id) == "number" and level.object_by_id(id) or nil
end

-- Host: runs fn as if `peer` had asked for it through a task request (give_task inside = its task).
function run_as(peer, fn, ...)
	local prev = host.exec_peer
	host.exec_peer = tonumber(peer) ~= 0 and tonumber(peer) or nil
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	host.exec_peer = prev
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

-- coop_story.cpp: a client asked through the engine requests (TaskReqGive / TaskReqState).
function host_note(id, kind, peer)
	peer = tonumber(peer)
	if type(id) ~= "string" or not peer then return end
	if kind == "taker" then
		host.taker_note[id] = peer
	elseif kind == "finisher" and host.finisher[id] == nil then
		host.finisher[id] = peer
	end
end

local function task_known(id)
	local ini = task_manager and task_manager.task_ini
	local ok, yes = pcall(function() return ini and ini:section_exist(id) end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function host_talking()
	local ok, yes = pcall(function() return db.actor:is_talking() end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function engine_task_running(id)
	local ok, t = pcall(function() return db.actor:get_task(id, true) end)
	return ok and t ~= nil
end

-- Host: a player's balance on the host ledger (coop.money_of), nil when the ledger does not answer.
local function ledger_money(peer)
	local fn = api and api.money_of
	if type(fn) ~= "function" then return nil end
	local ok, n = pcall(fn, peer)
	return ok and type(n) == "number" and n or nil
end

-- Host: the ledger balance of the client who took a task (nil: the host took it, or the ledger does not answer). The
-- host's own status functors read db.actor:money(), the host's: a money task a client took needs HIS money.
function taker_money(id)
	local peer = host.taker[id]
	if not is_host() or not peer or peer == 0 then return nil end
	return ledger_money(peer)
end

-- True if `peer` cannot pay the DRX money task `id` (its price is the task var "<id>_fetch").
local function money_short(tm, id, peer)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	if not (is_task(tsk) and tsk.status_functor == MONEY_FUNCTOR) then return false end
	local have = ledger_money(peer)
	return have ~= nil and have < (tonumber(load_var(db.actor, id .. "_fetch", 0)) or 0)
end

-- The wait of a "check_if_enough_time_passed" task is counted from the give. Its giving dialog saves the time right after
-- give_task, in the pstor of the machine that talks: a client's, where the host never sees it (a CTime cannot travel) and
-- the wait would end at once. The host stamps the give itself (over a time an earlier give of the client left in the vars).
-- (G.A.M.M.A. sets the wait of the helmet upgrade to 0; the stock task waits two days.)
local function stamp_wait(id, tsk)
	if not is_task(tsk) or tsk.status_functor ~= WAIT_FUNCTOR then return end
	local save_time = rawget(_G, "save_ctime")
	if type(save_time) == "function" then save_time(db.actor, id, game.get_game_time()) end
end

-- Client request handlers (host). Return true when accepted; the state is then broadcast by the scan.
local ops = {}

-- The player a request of a map server's logic belongs to: who took the task, else a player of its level. It is no player itself.
function player_of_request(from, id)
	if type(from) ~= "number" or from < 0x100 then return from end
	local l = api.levels
	local lid = nil
	for _, ms in ipairs(l and l.map_servers and l.map_servers() or {}) do
		if ms.bridge == from then lid = ms.level end
	end
	local taker_is = host.taker[id]
	if taker_is and taker_is ~= 0 and lid and l.level_of_player(taker_is) == lid then return taker_is end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if lid and l.level_of_player(p.id) == lid then return p.id end
	end
	return 0
end

-- Host: did player `from` talk to NPC `nid` a moment ago? The talk lock of a player on a map server's level is on that map server,
-- which reports it with his place (as coop_quests_missions talked_recently). An engine without the talk locks: yes.
function _spoke_to(from, nid)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if type(qc) == "table" and qc.is_far_peer and qc.is_far_peer(from) then
		local l = api.levels
		return l == nil or l.talking == nil or l.talking(from) == true
	end
	local recent = api.talk_recent
	if type(recent) ~= "function" then return true end
	return recent(from, nid, 15000) == true
end

function ops.give(tm, id, t, from)
	if tm.task_info[id] ~= nil and engine_task_running(id) then return false end
	local got_vars = {}
	if type(t.v) == "string" then
		for k, v in pairs(unpack_payload(t.v)) do
			if is_task_key(k, id) and var_value_ok(v) then
				save_var(db.actor, k, v)
				got_vars[k] = true
			end
		end
	end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(t.bt) == "number" then b[id] = t.bt end
	local giver = tonumber(t.g) -- host numbering == local numbering on the host
	host.taker[id] = from
	host.given_by[id] = from
	host.finisher[id] = nil
	host.giver = giver
	-- The NPC the player talks to is the speaker while the task starts: an on_init asks get_speaker() for him (setup_fetch_task of
	-- lttz_ll_medical_supplies died on nil: the quest audit, 2026-11-13). His word counts only if the host saw the talk.
	local sp = tonumber(t.sp)
	local npc = sp and sp ~= 0 and (db.storage[sp] and db.storage[sp].object or level.object_by_id(sp)) or nil
	if npc and not _spoke_to(from, sp) then npc = nil end
	local stock_speaker = rawget(_G, "get_speaker")
	if npc then _G.get_speaker = function() return npc end end
	local gave, gerr = pcall(tm.give_task, tm, id, giver)
	if npc then _G.get_speaker = stock_speaker end
	host.giver = nil
	if not gave then
		-- The stock puts the task object into task_info BEFORE its give_task runs on_init and gives the task to the actor
		-- (CRandomTask:give_task). An on_init that died leaves the object behind: a task of the journal that is no task of the
		-- engine. It was sent to every player as given and never judged ("the KMB does not update", owner 2026-11-13; seen on
		-- the stand 2026-11-14 with the guards of coop_quests_far taken out).
		if tm.task_info[id] ~= nil and not engine_task_running(id) then tm.task_info[id] = nil end
		error(gerr, 0)
	end
	local given = tm.task_info[id] ~= nil
	if given then
		stamp_wait(id, tm.task_info[id])
		-- host-side parts of the offer the client's dialog prepared (pinned target squads, ...)
		local qo = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_offer")
		if type(qo) == "table" and type(qo.host_after_give) == "function" then
			local ok, err = pcall(qo.host_after_give, id, from, giver, got_vars)
			if not ok then report("after give " .. id, err) end
		end
	end
	return given
end

local function finish(method)
	return function(tm, id, t, from)
		if tm.task_info[id] == nil or not engine_task_running(id) then return false end
		if method == "set_task_completed" and money_short(tm, id, from) then
			log("#%s cannot turn in '%s': not enough money", tostring(from), id)
			return false
		end
		if host.finisher[id] == nil then host.finisher[id] = from end
		tm[method](tm, id)
		return "pending" -- the task callback follows when the host checks its tasks
	end
end
ops.complete = finish("set_task_completed")
ops.fail = finish("set_task_failed")
ops.cancel = finish("set_task_cancelled")

function ops.stage(tm, id, t, from)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	local st = tonumber(t.st)
	-- a stage is a byte of the task object; 255 is the repeat timeout the host itself sets
	if tsk == nil or not st or st < 0 or st >= 255 or st ~= math_floor(st) then return false end
	tsk.stage = st
	return true
end

-- A client's active task (C8): check_level below brings the guide marker of his task.
function ops.active(tm, id, t, from)
	host.active[from] = not t.off and id or nil
	return "pending"
end

local function host_on_request(payload, from)
	if not is_host() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	stats.req_in = stats.req_in + 1
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local id, op = t.i, t.op
	local fn = type(op) == "string" and ops[op]
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or not fn or not task_known(id) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		log("! bad task request from #%s: %s %s", tostring(from), tostring(op), tostring(id))
		if type(id) == "string" and id ~= "" and #id <= 128 then host_send_state(id, from) end
		return
	end
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm then return end
	local who = player_of_request(from, id)
	host.exec_peer = who
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	local ok, res
	if qc and qc.with_level_of then
		ok, res = pcall(qc.with_level_of, who, fn, tm, id, t, who) -- his dialog, his NPC, his level
	else
		ok, res = pcall(fn, tm, id, t, who)
	end
	host.exec_peer = nil
	if not ok then report("request " .. op .. " " .. id, res) end
	if not ok or not res then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		if op == "give" and tm.task_info[id] == nil then
			-- A give this host could not do (its on_init died, the task said no) and no such task here: "not given" by name. The
			-- requester tells its player and frees the dialog that asked; a plain removal would drop his stub in silence.
			send(EV_STATE, pack({ i = id, d = true, r = 1 }), from)
			stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
		else
			host_send_state(id, from) -- the requester is behind: put its view back
		end
		return
	end
	log("#%s: %s '%s'", tostring(from), op, id)
	if res ~= "pending" then host_scan(false) end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: rewards to the player who turned the task in (R-7.6)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function rcpt_client()
	return ctx ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 and ctx.rcpt or nil
end

local function is_my_actor(obj)
	if obj == nil or not db.actor then return false end -- compared by id below: game_object has no == in luabind
	local ok, id = pcall(function()
		local f = obj.id
		if type(f) == "function" then return obj:id() end
		return f
	end)
	return ok and id == db.actor:id()
end

local function send_reward(peer, t)
	if t.t == nil and ctx then t.t = ctx.task end
	if send(EV_REWARD, pack(t), peer) then stats.rewards_routed = stats.rewards_routed + 1 end
end

-- The key of a player's waiting effects is his character, never a reusable peer slot.
local function effect_key(peer)
	return character_of(peer)
end

-- Host: an effect on a player's own character, run by his machine. It waits for his answer and goes out again on his next
-- sync: a level change or a reconnect right after the turn-in would lose it (client_on_reward needs an actor), and money
-- may already have been taken for it. The host's save keeps what waits (save_effects).
local function send_effect(peer, t)
	local key = effect_key(peer)
	if key == nil then report("effect", "recipient character is unknown"); return end
	host.fx_seq = host.fx_seq + 1
	t.q = host.fx_seq
	if t.t == nil and ctx then t.t = ctx.task end
	local map_server = api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server() == true
	if map_server then t.i, t.e = key, host.map_epoch end
	local s = pack(t)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[key]
	if not wait then
		wait = {}
		host.fx_wait[key] = wait
	end
	wait[#wait + 1] = { q = t.q, s = s }
	if map_server then send("coop_rep_map", s, 0); return end
	local online = peer_for_character(key)
	if online and online ~= 0 and send(EV_REWARD, s, online) then stats.rewards_routed = stats.rewards_routed + 1 end
end

local function host_on_effect_ack(payload, from)
	if not is_host() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	local q = tonumber(payload)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[effect_key(from)]
	if not (q and wait) then return end
	for i, e in ipairs(wait) do
		if e.q == q then
			table.remove(wait, i)
			return
		end
	end
end

local function host_resend_effects(peer)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[effect_key(peer)]
	if not wait then return end
	for _, e in ipairs(wait) do send(EV_REWARD, e.s, peer) end
end

-- Host: money for (or from, n < 0) a client's character. The money is the host ledger's (F2 T6): coop.money_grant
-- changes the character's money (never below 0) and the engine sends the client its new balance. A client's own
-- Lua never adds it: the engine would count that as the client's income, limited by the Script allowance, and a
-- reward above it would be lost. The client only gets the news line (event coop_trw, k = mn).
local function grant_money(peer, n)
	local whole = n >= 0 and math_floor(n) or -math_floor(-n)
	if whole ~= whole or whole == 0 or whole == math.huge or whole == -math.huge then return false end
	local grant = api and api.money_grant
	if type(grant) ~= "function" then
		report("grant_money", "coop.money_grant is missing")
		return false
	end
	local called, ok, why = pcall(grant, peer, whole)
	if not (called and ok) then
		log("money %d for #%s refused: %s", whole, tostring(peer), tostring(called and why or ok))
		return false
	end
	send_reward(peer, { k = "mn", n = whole })
	return true
end

function flush_fines()
	if not is_host() then return end
	for id, owed in pairs(host.fines) do
		local peer = peer_for_character(id)
		local balance = peer ~= nil and api.money_of and api.money_of(peer)
		if type(balance) == "number" then
			local amount = math.min(owed, math.max(0, balance))
			if amount == 0 or grant_money(peer, -amount) then host.fines[id] = nil end
		end
	end
end

-- Offline guide fines wait for that character; another player reusing his peer pays nothing.
function fine_character(id, amount)
	if not is_host() or type(id) ~= "number" or id < 0 or id >= 65535 or id % 1 ~= 0
		or type(amount) ~= "number" or amount ~= amount or amount <= 0 or amount == math.huge then return false end
	host.fines[id] = (host.fines[id] or 0) + math_floor(amount)
	flush_fines()
	return true
end

-- Host: the "money received" line on a player's machine for money the host changed outside a task reward (achievement
-- money, coop_quests_pda); the money itself is the ledger's.
function money_line(peer, n)
	if not is_host() then return false end
	n = tonumber(n)
	if not (n and peer ~= nil and tonumber(peer) ~= 0) then return false end
	send_reward(tonumber(peer), { k = "mn", n = n })
	return true
end

local function online_peers()
	-- peer 0 is the host player's character. A world server whose seat plays no character has only its ghost there: no share for it
	-- (the quest audit, 2026-11-13: with coop_share_rewards 1 the ghost took a part of every reward).
	local list = (api.is_dedicated and api.is_dedicated() == true) and {} or { 0 }
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self and p.avatar_id and (level.object_by_id(p.avatar_id) or far_of(p.id, p.avatar_id)) then list[#list + 1] = p.id end
	end
	if #list == 0 then list[1] = ctx and ctx.rcpt or 0 end -- nobody in the world to share with: the one who earned it
	return list
end

-- Host, in a reward scope: pays n to the player who turned the task in, or splits it over the online players
-- (coop_share_rewards 1; the remainder goes to the finisher). give(peer, amount) pays one share, peer 0 = the host.
local function split_money(n, give)
	if ctx.group then
		local rg = reward_group()
		for _, e in ipairs(rg.money_plan(n, ctx.group, ctx.rcpt, ctx.full)) do
			if e.m.in_world then give(e.m.peer, e.n) else rg.pay_absent(e.m, e.n) end
		end
		return
	end
	local list = ctx.share and online_peers() or { ctx.rcpt }
	local part = math_floor(n / #list)
	local rest = n - part * #list
	local rest_to = 0
	for _, peer in ipairs(list) do
		if peer == ctx.rcpt then rest_to = peer end
	end
	for _, peer in ipairs(list) do
		local amount = part + (peer == rest_to and rest or 0)
		if amount > 0 then give(peer, amount) end
	end
end

-- Stock payouts that do not go through dialogs.relocate_money but call db.actor:give_money themselves
-- (tasks_multifetch.remove_items_and_pay from multifetch_remove, tasks_defense.barrier_defense_*_complete) would put the
-- money on the HOST's actor whoever turned the task in (F2 T6 review). Their file cannot change, so the wrapper
-- (redirect_payout) measures what the call adds to the host's money, takes it back and pays it as every other task
-- money: to the player who turned the task in through the host ledger, or split with coop_share_rewards 1. The host
-- keeps it only when it turned the task in itself. While the call runs, the stock "money received" line for the host's
-- actor is swallowed (payout_scope): the player who gets the money sees his own line.
local payout_scope = false
local news_money = nil -- news_manager.relocate_money as it was before patch_rewards

local function redirect_payout(orig)
	return function(...)
		if not (ctx and (ctx.rcpt ~= 0 or ctx.share) and is_host() and db.actor) then return orig(...) end
		local before = db.actor:money()
		local prev = payout_scope
		payout_scope = true
		local res = { pcall(orig, ...) }
		payout_scope = prev
		local gained = db.actor:money() - before
		if gained > 0 and ctx then
			db.actor:give_money(-gained)
			split_money(gained, function(peer, amount)
				if peer == 0 then
					db.actor:give_money(amount)
					if news_money then news_money(db.actor, "in", amount) end
				else
					grant_money(peer, amount)
				end
			end)
		end
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		return unpack(res, 2)
	end
end

local FETCH_EFFECTS = { "fetch_reward_and_remove", "remove_fetch_item", "remove_artefact_item" }

-- Host: one unit of a group reward (coop_share_rewards 2, 3). The stock code that asked gets the item of the player who
-- turned the task in, if he got one.
local function give_to_group(create, section, t)
	local rg = reward_group()
	local res
	for _, m in ipairs(rg.item_targets(ctx.group, ctx.full)) do
		local owner = rg.holder(m)
		local se = owner and create(section, owner, t)
		if se then
			local g = ctx.given[m.id]
			if not g then
				g = { m = m, items = {} }
				ctx.given[m.id] = g
			end
			g.items[section] = (g.items[section] or 0) + 1
			ctx.counted[section] = true
			if res == nil or m.peer == ctx.rcpt then res = se end
		end
	end
	return res
end

-- Host, when (a part of) a group reward was handed out: one line per player and section, however many units the stock
-- code made. A player who is away gets a note instead.
local news_item = nil -- news_manager.relocate_item as it was before patch_rewards

local function group_lines(c)
	if not c.group then return end
	local rg = reward_group()
	for _, g in pairs(c.given) do
		for section, n in pairs(g.items) do
			if not g.m.in_world then
				rg.note_item(g.m.id, section, n)
			elseif g.m.peer == 0 then
				if news_item then news_item(db.actor, "in", section, n) end
			else
				send_reward(g.m.peer, { k = "news", ty = "in", s = section, n = n, t = c.task })
			end
		end
	end
	c.given = {}
	if c.noted then return end
	c.noted = true
	for _, m in ipairs(c.group) do
		if not m.in_world then rg.note(m.id, "c", 1) end
	end
end

local function host_task_callback(orig, tsk, state)
	local okid, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
	if not (is_host() and okid and type(id) == "string") or not (state == task.completed or state == task.fail) then
		return orig(tsk, state)
	end
	local rcpt = recipient(id)
	local owner = rcpt -- statistics, rank and reputation: his, also when he has left (they wait for him)
	-- messages: the player who asked for this result (nil: a script, a timer), and whether it was a cancel
	local by = host.finisher[id]
	local tm = tmgr()
	local rtask = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
	local cancelled = is_task(rtask) and rtask.cancelled_by_actor == true
	host.finisher[id] = nil
	local mode = state == task.completed and reward_mode() or 0
	local share = mode ~= 0
	local everyone = mode == EVERYONE_SHARED or mode == EVERYONE_FULL
	-- W5: also for the host's own task (rcpt 0): without the reward scope the story wrapper
	-- (coop_quests_story) took its on_complete rewards for a story condlist and paid every client too
	local prev = ctx
	ctx = { task = id, rcpt = rcpt, share = share, by = by, cancelled = cancelled, owner = owner }
	ctx.character = by == nil and host.taker_char[id] or character_of(rcpt)
	if not cancelled then
		if state == task.fail then
			ctx.personal = host.failure_participants[id]
		elseif rep_share_rule() == "everyone" then
			-- each character once: the taker, who was in game at the accept, who is in game now
			local ids, seen = {}, {}
			local function put(list)
				for _, c in ipairs(list or {}) do
					if type(c) == "number" and not seen[c] then ids[#ids + 1], seen[c] = c, true end
				end
			end
			put({ host.taker_char[id] })
			put(host.rep_party[id] or host.participants[id])
			put(participant_ids())
			ctx.personal = #ids > 0 and ids or nil
		end
		if ctx.personal == nil and host.taker_char[id] ~= nil then ctx.personal = { host.taker_char[id] } end
	end
	if everyone then
		ctx.group, ctx.full = reward_group().list(), mode == EVERYONE_FULL
		ctx.given, ctx.counted = {}, {}
	end
	local this = ctx
	-- The stock end of a task (on_complete, on_fail, on_cancel and what they call) reads the world around "the actor": the giver's
	-- game object (goodwill by the tasker), the quest item to take away, the actor's faction (the next DRX giver), the first target of
	-- the task it gives next. On a world server that world is a map server's level, and "at home" none of it was found (the quest
	-- audit, 2026-11-13). The end runs in the far view of the level of the player it is for - he stands at the giver when he turns
	-- the task in - and, with nobody to name (a timer, a script), on the level of what the task is about. Without split levels the
	-- far view is no view: the call is the stock's.
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	local ok, err
	if not (qc and qc.with_level_of and qc.with_target) then
		ok, err = pcall(orig, tsk, state)
	elseif rcpt ~= 0 then
		ok, err = pcall(qc.with_level_of, rcpt, orig, tsk, state)
	else
		local about = is_task(rtask) and (type(rtask.current_target) == "number" and rtask.current_target or rtask.task_giver_id) or nil
		ok, err = pcall(qc.with_target, about, 0, id, orig, tsk, state)
	end
	ctx = prev
	group_lines(this)
	host.given_by[id] = nil
	if not ok then report("task callback " .. id, err) end
	if rcpt ~= 0 then log("rewards of '%s' go to #%s%s", id, tostring(rcpt), share and " (money shared)" or "") end
end

-- The client whose character the rank and reputation being changed now belong to, or nil: the host's.
local function stat_peer()
	-- Peer zero on a map server is the real host player, not this process's ghost actor.
	if ctx and ctx.character == 0 and api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server() then return 0 end
	local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
	if ctx == nil and p and p.in_identity and p.in_identity() then
		local peer = p.peer_of(db.actor)
		if peer ~= nil then return peer ~= 0 and peer or nil end
	end
	if ctx == nil then return nil end
	if ctx.owner ~= nil and ctx.owner ~= 0 then return ctx.owner end
	return rcpt_client()
end

-- Client peer the effects being run now are keyed to (items into its character, news to it), or nil.
function reward_peer()
	return ctx ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 and ctx.rcpt or nil
end

function personal_character()
	return ctx and ctx.character
end

function active_of(peer)
	return host.active[peer]
end

-- True while a task's rewards / status effects are being handed out (they belong to one player).
function in_reward_scope()
	return ctx ~= nil
end

-- Host: runs fn with the effects keyed to the actor (items, news, money, goodwill) going to `peer`.
function with_recipient(peer, fn, ...)
	peer = tonumber(peer)
	if not is_host() and not (active() and api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server()) then return fn(...) end
	if not peer or peer < 0 or peer % 1 ~= 0 then
		report("recipient", "missing or invalid player; personal effects were not applied")
		return
	end
	-- A player can be loading or disconnected while a timer fires. Keep his address:
	-- send_effect persists statistics until he acknowledges them. Never substitute the host.
	-- An explicit nested scope (including peer 0) must temporarily replace the outer recipient.
	local id, previous = character_of(peer), ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer, owner = peer, character = id, share = false, status = true }
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = previous
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

function with_character(id, fn, ...)
	if type(id) ~= "number" or id < 0 then return end
	local peer, previous = peer_for_character(id), ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer or -1, owner = peer or -1,
		character = id, share = false, status = true }
	local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
	local result
	if id == 0 and p and p.in_identity and p.in_identity() then
		result = { pcall(p.with_identity, p.own_actor(), fn, ...) }
	else result = { pcall(fn, ...) } end
	ctx = previous
	if not result[1] then error(result[2], 0) end
	return unpack(result, 2)
end

function each_personal(fn, ...)
	if not (ctx and ctx.personal and #ctx.personal > 0) then return false end
	for _, id in ipairs(ctx.personal) do with_character(id, fn, ...) end
	return true
end

-- Execute world logic once, distributing only its personal reputation/statistic/goodwill effects.
function with_participants(ids, peer, fn, ...)
	if not is_host() and not (active() and api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server()) then return fn(...) end
	local previous = ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer or 0, owner = peer or 0,
		character = character_of(peer or 0), personal = ids, share = false, status = true }
	local result = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = previous
	if not result[1] then error(result[2], 0) end
	return unpack(result, 2)
end

-- Host: a task's status / target functors run with the actor's effects going to the player who took it
-- (a measuring device handed out on the first check lands in that player's character).
function with_task_owner(id, fn, ...)
	if ctx ~= nil or not is_host() or type(id) ~= "string" then return fn(...) end
	local t = host.taker[id]
	if t == nil then return fn(...) end
	ctx = { task = id, rcpt = t, owner = t, character = host.taker_char[id] or character_of(t), share = false, status = true,
		personal = host.participants[id] }
	-- a functor can make a companion by writing the stock table itself (tasks_agent_rescue): what it added is the taker's
	local comp = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_companions")
	local before = comp and comp.squads_now and comp.squads_now()
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = nil
	if before then comp.claim_since(before, t) end
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

-- Stock effects read the actor of the machine they run on: statistics, rank and reputation of a task (the counters of
-- task_manager.task_callback, increase_rank and the like in on_complete, tasks_guide) would all land on the host's actor.
local function patch_statistics()
	local gs = rawget(_G, "game_statistics") or game_statistics
	if type(gs) ~= "table" then
		log("! game_statistics not found: a task's rank and reputation stay on the host's actor")
		return
	end
	-- owner 2026-11-13: what is no player's here would land on the ghost actor of a map server or of a world server whose seat plays
	-- no character (coop_quests_core.actor_is_nobody): dropped. An ordinary host's actor is its player: unchanged.
	local function nobody()
		local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core") or coop_quests_core
		return qc ~= nil and qc.actor_is_nobody ~= nil and qc.actor_is_nobody() == true
	end
	local count = gs.increment_statistic
	if type(count) == "function" then
		gs.increment_statistic = function(name, custom_rank, custom_rept)
			if TASK_STATS[name] and each_personal(gs.increment_statistic, name, custom_rank, custom_rept) then return end
			local peer = stat_peer()
			if not peer and nobody() then return end
			if not peer then return count(name, custom_rank, custom_rept) end
			send_effect(peer, { k = "stat", f = name, r = tonumber(custom_rank), p = tonumber(custom_rept) })
		end
	end
	for fname, what in pairs({ increment_rank = "rank", increment_reputation = "rept" }) do
		local orig = gs[fname]
		if type(orig) == "function" then
			gs[fname] = function(value)
				if what == "rept" and each_personal(gs[fname], value) then return end
				local peer = stat_peer()
				if not peer and nobody() then return end
				if not peer then return orig(value) end
				send_effect(peer, { k = "stat", f = what, n = tonumber(value) or 0 })
			end
		end
	end
end

-- The "stash coordinates" line of a task's reward is the player's who turned it in (the spot is everybody's). The line
-- is shown inside set_random_stash; a mod's override may add a text, the client computes that one in its own language.
local function patch_stash_line()
	local tm = rawget(_G, "treasure_manager") or treasure_manager
	if not (type(tm) == "table" and type(tm.set_random_stash) == "function") then
		log("! treasure_manager.set_random_stash not found: stash lines of task rewards stay on the host")
		return
	end
	local orig = tm.set_random_stash
	tm.set_random_stash = function(no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg)
		local peer = rcpt_client()
		local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
		local stock = nm and nm.send_treasure
		if not (peer and type(stock) == "function") then return orig(no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg) end
		local told = false
		nm.send_treasure = function(param, text)
			if param == 0 or param == nil then told = true else return stock(param, text) end
		end
		local res = { pcall(orig, no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg) }
		nm.send_treasure = stock
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
		if told and type(qc) == "table" then qc.send("treasure", { p = 0, b = tonumber(res[2]) or tonumber(id) }, peer) end
		return unpack(res, 2)
	end
end

local function patch_rewards()
	-- a restrictor's condlist gives a task: the effect knows the zone (nearest_taker)
	local xfx = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xfx and type(xfx.give_task) == "function" then
		local give = xfx.give_task
		xfx.give_task = function(actor, obj, p)
			local prev = host.give_near
			host.give_near = obj
			local res = { pcall(give, actor, obj, p) }
			host.give_near = prev
			if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
			return unpack(res, 2)
		end
	end

	-- money
	local dlg = rawget(_G, "dialogs") or dialogs
	if dlg and type(dlg.relocate_money) == "function" then
		local orig = dlg.relocate_money
		dlg.relocate_money = function(victim, num, typ)
			local n = tonumber(num)
			if not (ctx and typ == "in" and n and n > 0) then return orig(victim, num, typ) end
			split_money(n, function(peer, amount)
				if peer == 0 then
					orig(victim, amount, "in")
				else
					grant_money(peer, amount)
				end
			end)
		end
	else
		log("! dialogs.relocate_money not found: task money is not routed")
	end

	-- items into the turning-in player's character (host-authoritative spawn)
	local create = rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	if type(create) == "function" then
		raw_create = create
		_G.alife_create_item = function(section, obj, t)
			if ctx and ctx.group and not ctx.returns and is_my_actor(obj) and reward_group().shareable(section) then
				return give_to_group(create, section, t)
			end
			local peer = rcpt_client()
			if peer and is_my_actor(obj) then
				local o = recipient_body(peer)
				if o then return create(section, o, t) end
				report("item reward", "recipient character unavailable: " .. tostring(character_of(peer)))
				return -- never create a client's item in the host's inventory
			end
			return create(section, obj, t)
		end
	else
		log("! alife_create_item not found: task items are not routed")
	end

	-- xr_effects.give_actor (the PDA of a task, in its on_init) makes the item with alife_create(section, ..., AC_ID): past the
	-- redirect above, into the host's own inventory, which on a world server is its ghost's (the quest audit, 2026-11-13). For a
	-- task of another player the item is made the routed way; the host's own task is the stock's.
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xe and type(xe.give_actor) == "function" then
		local stock_give = xe.give_actor
		xe.give_actor = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (rcpt_client() and type(p) == "table") then return stock_give(actor, npc, p) end
			local news = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
			for _, section in pairs(p) do
				alife_create_item(section, db.actor)
				if news and news.relocate_item then news.relocate_item(db.actor, "in", section) end
			end
		end
	end

	-- xr_effects.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm takes the giver's faction from the task's var (task_giver_comm: only the delivery
	-- tasks write it) or from the NPC the actor talks to. A task a client turns in ends in the host's task callback, where nobody
	-- talks: 15 tasks gave no goodwill (the quest audit, 2026-11-13). The faction of the task's giver, from his record, stands
	-- in the var for this one call; a faction the task wrote itself and the host's own talk are the stock's.
	local stock_comm = xe and xe.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm
	if type(stock_comm) == "function" then
		xe.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm = function(actor, npc, p)
			local id = type(p) == "table" and p[1]
			local tm = type(id) == "string" and is_host() and tmgr() or nil
			local tsk = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
			if not (tsk and db.actor) or db.actor:is_talking() then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local had = load_var(db.actor, id)
			if type(had) == "table" and had.task_giver_comm then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local se = tsk.task_giver_id and rawget(_G, "alife_object") and alife_object(tsk.task_giver_id)
			local ok, comm = pcall(function() return se and se:community() end)
			if not (ok and type(comm) == "string" and comm ~= "") then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local with = {}
			if type(had) == "table" then
				for k, v in pairs(had) do with[k] = v end
			end
			with.task_giver_comm = comm
			save_var(db.actor, id, with)
			local res = { pcall(stock_comm, actor, npc, p) }
			save_var(db.actor, id, had)
			if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
			return unpack(res, 2)
		end
	end

	-- item news to the player who gets / gives the items
	local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
	if nm and type(nm.relocate_item) == "function" then
		local orig = nm.relocate_item
		news_item = orig
		nm.relocate_item = function(actor, typ, item, amount)
			if ctx and ctx.group and ctx.counted[item] and typ == "in" and is_my_actor(actor) then return true end -- group_lines
			local peer = rcpt_client()
			if peer and is_my_actor(actor) then
				send_reward(peer, { k = "news", ty = tostring(typ), s = tostring(item), n = tonumber(amount) or 1 })
				return true
			end
			return orig(actor, typ, item, amount)
		end
	end

	if nm and type(nm.relocate_money) == "function" then
		news_money = nm.relocate_money
		nm.relocate_money = function(actor, typ, amount)
			if payout_scope and is_my_actor(actor) then return true end -- the player who gets the money sees the line
			return news_money(actor, typ, amount)
		end
	end

	-- goodwill rewards / penalties keyed to the player's own character
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xe then
		for _, fname in ipairs({ "inc_faction_goodwill_to_actor", "dec_faction_goodwill_to_actor" }) do
			local orig = xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(actor, npc, p)
					if is_my_actor(actor) and each_personal(xe[fname], actor, npc, p) then return end
					local peer = rcpt_client()
					if peer and type(p) == "table" and is_my_actor(actor) then
						local o = recipient_body(peer)
						if o then
							local r = orig(o, npc, { p[1], p[2] }) -- no message on the host
							if p[3] and p[1] then
								send_reward(peer, { k = "gw", c = tostring(p[1]),
									g = fname == "inc_faction_goodwill_to_actor" and (tonumber(p[2]) or 0) > 0 })
							end
							return r
						end
						report("goodwill", "recipient character unavailable: " .. tostring(character_of(peer)))
						return
					end
					return orig(actor, npc, p)
				end
			end
		end
		-- payment for a money task: taken from the player who turned it in
		local pay = xe.drx_sl_money_task_payment
		if type(pay) == "function" then
			xe.drx_sl_money_task_payment = function(actor, npc, p)
				local peer = rcpt_client()
				if peer and type(p) == "table" and p[1] ~= nil then
					local money = tonumber(load_var(db.actor, p[1], 0)) or 0
					local have = money > 0 and ledger_money(peer) or nil
					if have and have < money then
						-- spent since the turn-in: the ledger would stop at 0 and the faction change would be free
						ctx.unpaid = true
						log("'%s': #%s has %d RU, the task takes %d: not paid", tostring(ctx.task), tostring(peer), have, money)
						return
					end
					if money > 0 then grant_money(peer, -money) end
					return
				end
				return pay(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
		-- Stock fetch effects take the player's goods and hand back what is left of them: the artefact out of its container,
		-- the empty container, the leftover uses. That is no reward: the group gets no copies of it.
		local fetch_module = _G.tasks_fetch -- it adds these effects to xr_effects when it loads: loads it now
		for _, fname in ipairs(FETCH_EFFECTS) do
			local orig = fetch_module ~= false and xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(...)
					if not (ctx and ctx.group) then return orig(...) end
					local c, prev = ctx, ctx.returns
					c.returns = true
					local res = { pcall(orig, ...) }
					c.returns = prev
					if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
					return unpack(res, 2)
				end
			end
		end
		-- tasks_multifetch pays on_complete with db.actor:give_money (the host's actor): to the one who turned it in
		if type(xe.multifetch_remove) == "function" then xe.multifetch_remove = redirect_payout(xe.multifetch_remove) end
		-- effects on the player's own character run on that player's machine
		for fname in pairs(FORWARD_EFFECTS) do
			local orig = xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(actor, npc, p)
					local peer = rcpt_client()
					if ctx and ctx.character == 0 and api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server() then peer = 0 end
					if peer and ctx.unpaid then
						log("'%s': %s skipped, the task was not paid", tostring(ctx.task), fname)
						return
					end
					if peer and type(p) == "table" then
						local t = { k = "fx", f = fname }
						for i = 1, 4 do
							if p[i] ~= nil then t["p" .. i] = tostring(p[i]) end
						end
						send_effect(peer, t)
						return
					end
					return orig(actor, npc, p)
				end
			end
		end
	end

	-- Freedom barrier defense pays 40 000 / 25 000 with db.actor:give_money from a dialog action (the speaker's
	-- machine). A client's own run is not touched (the engine ledger takes its change); when the host runs it for a
	-- player (with_recipient) the money goes to that player. The host's own talk pays the host.
	local td = rawget(_G, "tasks_defense") or tasks_defense
	if type(td) == "table" then
		for _, fname in ipairs({ "barrier_defense_monolith_complete", "barrier_defense_zombie_complete" }) do
			if type(td[fname]) == "function" then td[fname] = redirect_payout(td[fname]) end
		end
	end

	-- delayed rewards (fetch pays one second later) keep the context
	local cte = rawget(_G, "CreateTimeEvent")
	if type(cte) == "function" then
		_G.CreateTimeEvent = function(ev_id, act_id, timer, f, ...)
			if ctx and type(f) == "function" then
				local c, f0, returns = ctx, f, ctx.returns
				f = function(...)
					local prev = ctx
					ctx = c
					-- the group may have changed since the task was turned in; a return stays one a second later
					local prev_returns = c.returns
					c.returns = returns
					if c.group then c.group = reward_group().list() end
					local res = { pcall(f0, ...) }
					c.returns = prev_returns
					ctx = prev
					group_lines(c)
					if not res[1] then
						report("delayed task reward", res[2])
						return true
					end
					return unpack(res, 2)
				end
			end
			return cte(ev_id, act_id, timer, f, ...)
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: quest items of any group member (R-7.5)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Holders to take items from: the player who turned the task in first, then the host, then the rest.
local function holders()
	local list, rest = {}, {}
	local rc = rcpt_client()
	local mine
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if h.self then
			mine = h
		elseif rc and h.peer == rc then
			list[#list + 1] = h
		else
			rest[#rest + 1] = h
		end
	end
	if mine then list[#list + 1] = mine end
	for _, h in ipairs(rest) do list[#list + 1] = h end
	return list
end

-- Releases up to `amt` items of `sec` held by h (each item counts 1, like xr_effects.remove_item).
local function release_from(h, sec, amt)
	local ids = {}
	pcall(function()
		h.obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if #ids < amt and item:section() == sec then ids[#ids + 1] = item:id() end
		end, nil)
	end)
	for _, id in ipairs(ids) do alife_release_id(id) end
	if not h.self then stats.party_releases = stats.party_releases + #ids end
	return #ids
end

-- Moves up to `units` of `sec` from h to the host's actor (they arrive before a delayed stock reward runs).
local function move_from(h, sec, units)
	local moved = 0
	local multi = uses_of(sec)
	local items = {}
	pcall(function()
		h.obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if moved < units and item:section() == sec then
				items[#items + 1] = item
				moved = moved + (multi and item:get_remaining_uses() or 1)
			end
		end, nil)
	end)
	for _, item in ipairs(items) do h.obj:transfer_item(item, db.actor) end
	stats.party_moves = stats.party_moves + #items
	return moved
end

local function container_of(h, sec)
	for _, cont in ipairs(CONTAINERS) do
		local c = h.obj:object(sec .. "_" .. cont)
		if c then return c, cont end
	end
	return nil
end

local function host_party_on() return is_host() and has_clients() end

-- Spawn without the reward redirect (the item goes exactly where asked).
local function create_plain(sec, obj)
	local f = raw_create or rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	return f(sec, obj)
end

local function count_items(obj, sec) -- items, not uses
	local n = 0
	pcall(function()
		obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if item:section() == sec then n = n + 1 end
		end, nil)
	end)
	return n
end

local function party_remove(sec, amt)
	local left = amt
	for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
		if left <= 0 then break end
		left = left - release_from(h, sec, left)
	end
	local removed = amt - left
	if removed > 0 then news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, removed) end
	if left > 0 then log("! group had %d x %s less than the task takes", left, sec) end
	return removed
end

-- Host: takes up to `amt` items of `sec` from the group (the player the effects are keyed to first,
-- then the host, then the others). Returns how many were taken.
function party_take(sec, amt)
	if not is_host() or type(sec) ~= "string" then return 0 end
	amt = tonumber(amt) or 1
	if amt <= 0 then return 0 end
	local ok, n = pcall(party_remove, sec, amt)
	if not ok then
		report("party_take " .. sec, n)
		return 0
	end
	return n or 0
end

-- Host: a db.actor:iterate_inventory for ONE call (coop_quests_core.with_actor) that walks every player's character: the
-- turning-in player's first, then the host's, then the rest. Stock tasks_multifetch counts, pays for and takes items through
-- db.actor:iterate_inventory and releases them by id, so the group's items count and go like the host's own.
-- real = the plain method of db.actor. f(item_owner, item) returning true stops the walk, as in the engine.
function party_inventory_walker(real)
	return function(me, f, x)
		local stop = false
		local function g(owner, item)
			local r = f(owner, item)
			if r == true then stop = true end
			return r
		end
		for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
			if h.self then real(me, g, x) else h.obj:iterate_inventory(g, x) end
			if stop then return end
		end
	end
end

-- Host: money and items for one player (0 = the host's own actor). Items are spawned by the host into
-- that player's character; the player sees the news on its own machine.
function give_to_peer(peer, money, sections)
	if not is_host() and not (active() and api.is_map_server ~= nil and api.is_map_server() == true) then return end
	peer = tonumber(peer) or 0
	money = math_floor(tonumber(money) or 0)
	local mine = peer == 0 or peer == self_peer()
	if money ~= 0 then
		if mine then
			if money > 0 then dialogs.relocate_money(db.actor, money, "in") else db.actor:give_money(money) end
		else
			grant_money(peer, money)
		end
	end
	if type(sections) == "table" then
		local obj = mine and db.actor or avatar_obj(peer)
		for _, sec in ipairs(sections) do
			if type(sec) == "string" and sec ~= "" and obj then
				create_plain(sec, obj)
				if mine then
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "in", sec, 1)
				else
					send_reward(peer, { k = "news", ty = "in", s = sec, n = 1 })
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Fetch reward (stock: one second later, from the host's inventory): bring the items to the host's actor,
-- the turning-in player's own items first.
local function gather_fetch(var)
	local sec = load_var(db.actor, var)
	if type(sec) ~= "string" then return end
	local need = tonumber(load_var(db.actor, var .. "_count")) or 1
	local left = need
	local rc = rcpt_client()
	local list = holders()
	if rc and list[1] and list[1].peer == rc then left = left - move_from(list[1], sec, left) end
	left = left - count_in(db.actor, sec)
	for _, h in ipairs(list) do
		if left <= 0 then break end
		if not h.self and h.peer ~= rc then left = left - move_from(h, sec, left) end
	end
	-- an artefact asked for may sit in a container another player carries
	if left > 0 and sec:find("af_", 1, true) then
		for _, h in ipairs(list) do
			if left <= 0 then break end
			if not h.self then
				local c, cont = container_of(h, sec)
				if c then
					alife_release_id(c:id())
					create_plain(sec, db.actor)
					create_plain(cont, h.obj) -- the empty container stays with its owner
					left = left - 1
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function patch_party_items()
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if not xe then return end

	local remove_item = xe.remove_item
	if type(remove_item) == "function" then
		xe.remove_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (host_party_on() and type(p) == "table" and type(p[1]) == "string") then
				return remove_item(actor, npc, p)
			end
			local amt = tonumber(p[2]) or 1
			if not rcpt_client() and count_items(db.actor, p[1]) >= amt then return remove_item(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, err = pcall(party_remove, p[1], amt)
			if not ok then
				report("remove_item " .. p[1], err)
				return remove_item(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
	end

	local remove_fetch = xe.remove_fetch_item
	if type(remove_fetch) == "function" then
		xe.remove_fetch_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (host_party_on() and type(p) == "table" and p[1]) then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local sec = load_var(db.actor, p[1])
			if type(sec) ~= "string" then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local amt = tonumber(p[2]) or tonumber(load_var(db.actor, p[1] .. "_count")) or 1
			if not rcpt_client() and count_items(db.actor, sec) >= amt then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, err = pcall(party_remove, sec, amt)
			if not ok then
				report("remove_fetch_item " .. sec, err)
				return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
	end

	local remove_art = xe.remove_artefact_item
	if type(remove_art) == "function" then
		-- true when one artefact (or its container) was taken from somebody in the group
		local function party_remove_art(sec)
			for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
				if release_from(h, sec, 1) > 0 then
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, 1)
					return true
				end
				local c, cont = container_of(h, sec)
				if c then
					alife_release_id(c:id())
					create_plain(cont, h.obj) -- the empty container stays with its owner
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, 1)
					return true
				end
			end
			return false
		end
		xe.remove_artefact_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (host_party_on() and type(p) == "table" and p[1]) then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local sec = load_var(db.actor, p[1])
			if type(sec) ~= "string" then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local mine = { obj = db.actor, self = true }
			if not rcpt_client() and (db.actor:object(sec) or container_of(mine, sec)) then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, done = pcall(party_remove_art, sec)
			if not ok then report("remove_artefact_item " .. sec, done) end
			if ok and done then return end
			return remove_art(actor, npc, p)
		end
	end

	-- tasks_multifetch: its effects count and take through db.actor:iterate_inventory (the check is in coop_quests_party)
	for _, name in ipairs({ "multifetch_remove", "multifetch_task_trigger_extra_items_condlist" }) do
		local stock = xe[name]
		if type(stock) == "function" then
			xe[name] = function(...)
				local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
				local qp = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_party")
				if not (host_party_on() and db.actor and qc and type(qc.with_actor) == "function")
					or (qp and type(qp.checking_task) == "function" and qp.checking_task()) then
					return stock(...)
				end
				local fields = { iterate_inventory = party_inventory_walker(db.actor.iterate_inventory) }
				local res = { qc.with_actor(fields, stock, ...) }
				if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
				return unpack(res, 2)
			end
		end
	end

	local fetch_reward = xe.fetch_reward_and_remove
	if type(fetch_reward) == "function" then
		xe.fetch_reward_and_remove = function(actor, npc, p)
			if host_party_on() and type(p) == "table" and p[1] then
				local ok, err = pcall(gather_fetch, p[1])
				if not ok then report("fetch gather " .. tostring(p[1]), err) end
			end
			return fetch_reward(actor, npc, p)
		end
	end

	-- status functors: the task is ready to turn in when the group has the items
	local tsf = rawget(_G, "task_status_functor")
	if type(tsf) ~= "table" then
		log("! task_status_functor not found: quest items count only from the host's inventory")
		return
	end
	local function wrap_status(name, after)
		local orig = tsf[name]
		if type(orig) ~= "function" then return end
		tsf[name] = function(tsk, task_id)
			local r = orig(tsk, task_id)
			if r == nil and host_party_on() and tsk and tsk.stage ~= 1 then
				local ok, err = pcall(after, tsk, task_id)
				if not ok then report("status " .. name, err) end
			end
			return r
		end
	end
	wrap_status("actor_has_fetch_item", function(tsk, task_id)
		local sec = load_var(db.actor, task_id .. "_fetch")
		if type(sec) ~= "string" then return end
		local need = tonumber(load_var(db.actor, task_id .. "_fetch_count")) or 1
		local min_cond = FETCH_MIN_COND[task_id]
		local n = party_count(sec, min_cond)
		if not min_cond and sec:find("af_", 1, true) then
			for _, cont in ipairs(CONTAINERS) do n = n + party_count(sec .. "_" .. cont) end
		end
		if n >= need then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
	wrap_status("actor_has_fetch_weapon_warfare", function(tsk, task_id)
		local sec = load_var(db.actor, task_id .. "_fetch")
		if type(sec) == "string" and party_count(sec, 0.6) > 0 then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
	wrap_status("drx_sl_quest_item_task_status", function(tsk, task_id)
		local var = load_var(db.actor, task_id)
		if type(var) == "table" and var.stash_created and var.stash_type
			and party_count("drx_sl_quest_item_" .. tostring(var.stash_type)) > 0 then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Client: mirrored task stubs
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local cl = {
	recv = {}, -- id -> last state string from the host
	vars = {}, -- id -> { key = true } mirrored into our pstor
	synced = false,
	next_sync = 0,
	next_check = 0,
	full = nil, -- { gen, got, seen } the whole shared set while its parts arrive
	list = nil, -- { gen, got, listed, differ } the digest list while its parts arrive
	active = nil, -- the active task the host knows about
	want_active = nil, -- { id, at } a task this player asked for, to make active when it arrives
	fx_done = {}, -- q -> true: effects that ran here (a sync crossing the answer sends one again)
	lang_told = false,
}

local client_request -- forward

local STUB_METHODS = {
	check_task = function() end,
	give_task = function() end,
	give_reward = function() end,
	reverse_task = function() end,
	deactivate_task = function() end,
	check_level = function() end,
	remove_guider_spot = function() end,
	save = function() end,
	load = function() end,
	load_state = function() return false end,
	get_title = function(self) return self.title or "" end,
	get_icon_name = function(self) return self.icon end,
	-- Saved like a real task, so a game saved from this world after the session (if ever) still knows it.
	save_state = function(self, m_data)
		if type(m_data) ~= "table" or type(m_data.task_objects) ~= "table" then return end
		m_data.task_objects[self.id] = {
			status = self.status, stage = self.stage, task_giver_id = self.task_giver_id,
		}
	end,
}

local function stub_data(t)
	if type(t) ~= "table" then return nil end
	local mt = getmetatable(t)
	return type(mt) == "table" and mt.__coop_data or nil
end

local function engine_task(id)
	local a = db and db.actor
	if not a then return nil end
	local ok, t = pcall(a.get_task, a, id, true)
	return ok and t or nil
end

local function task_is_story(id)
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local ini = mod and mod.task_ini
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return ini:r_bool_ex(id, "storyline", false) end)
	return ok and v == true
end

-- What a real task object has and a stub can answer from the engine's copy (the GAMMA task monitor and HUD marks read them).
-- The engine's task type has no getter in Lua: the storyline flag comes from the task's config, as in CGeneralTask.
local STUB_FIELDS = {
	t = function(data) return engine_task(data.id) end,
	current_target = function(data)
		local t = engine_task(data.id)
		local ok, oid = pcall(function() return t and t:get_map_object_id() end)
		return ok and type(oid) == "number" and oid ~= 65535 and oid or nil
	end,
	storyline = function(data) return task_is_story(data.id) end,
}

-- A dialog script writing a stub field the host owns: the host does it.
local function on_stub_write(data, k, v)
	if not client_live() then return end
	if k == "stage" and type(v) == "number" then
		client_request("stage", data.id, { st = v })
	elseif k == "forced_status" and (v == "complete" or v == "fail") then
		client_request(v == "complete" and "complete" or "fail", data.id)
	elseif k == "cancelled_by_actor" and v == true then
		client_request("cancel", data.id)
	end
end

local function new_stub(id)
	local data = { id = id, coop_stub = true, stage = 0, status = "selected" }
	local mt = { __coop_data = data }
	mt.__index = function(_, k)
		local v = data[k]
		if v ~= nil then return v end
		local f = STUB_FIELDS[k]
		if f then return f(data) end
		return STUB_METHODS[k]
	end
	mt.__newindex = function(_, k, v)
		local old = data[k]
		data[k] = v
		if old ~= v then
			local ok, err = pcall(on_stub_write, data, k, v)
			if not ok then report("stub write", err) end
		end
	end
	return setmetatable({}, mt), data
end

local function clear_vars(id, keep)
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	local old = cl.vars[id]
	cl.vars[id] = nil
	if ps and old then
		for k in pairs(old) do
			local held = keep and keep[k] ~= nil
			for _, keys in pairs(cl.vars) do held = held or keys[k] == true end -- "a_b_x" is also a var of task "a_b"
			if not held then ps[k] = nil end
		end
	end
end

local function apply_vars(id, vars)
	clear_vars(id, vars)
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not ps then return end
	local keys = {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		if is_task_key(k, id) then
			ps[k] = v
			keys[k] = true
		end
	end
	cl.vars[id] = keys
end

-- The items of a multifetch task, for the stock inventory marks (fetch_item_icon reads alife_storage_manager's state,
-- on a client the join save's). tasks_multifetch keeps them in a local table; they come from the task's config, the same
-- on every machine.
local function multifetch_items(ini, id, kind)
	local out = {}
	local i = 1
	while ini:line_exist(id, kind .. "_item_" .. i) do
		out[i] = { sec = ini:r_string_ex(id, kind .. "_item_" .. i) }
		i = i + 1
	end
	return out
end

local function mirror_multifetch(id, on)
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local ini = mod and mod.task_ini
	local asm = rawget(_G, "alife_storage_manager") or alife_storage_manager
	if not (ini and asm and asm.get_state) then return end
	local st = asm.get_state()
	if type(st) ~= "table" then return end
	if not on then
		if type(st.multifetch_data) == "table" then st.multifetch_data[id] = nil end
		return
	end
	if ini:r_string_ex(id, "status_functor") ~= "multifetch_status_functor" then return end
	st.multifetch_data = st.multifetch_data or {}
	st.multifetch_data[id] = { required_items = multifetch_items(ini, id, "required"),
		optional_items = multifetch_items(ini, id, "optional") }
end

local function forget_task(tm, id)
	tm.task_info[id] = nil
	cl.recv[id] = nil
	clear_vars(id)
	local ok, err = pcall(mirror_multifetch, id, false)
	if not ok then report("multifetch " .. id, err) end
end

-- The infos of the dialog phrase that asked for a task. The engine runs a phrase's actions first and gives its <give_info> after
-- them, in the same frame (CDialogScriptHelper::Action): an info the actor gets in the frame of a give asked from a talk is the
-- phrase's, and it is kept with the provisional stub.
function _client_on_info(npc, info)
	local a = cl.asking
	if not a or a.at ~= now() or type(info) ~= "string" then return end
	for _, data in ipairs(a.stubs) do
		local list = data.phrase_infos
		if list and #list < 8 then list[#list + 1] = info end
	end
end

-- The host could not give the task this player asked for ("The Last Dawn", 2026-11-13: the give died in the task's on_init, the stub
-- vanished in silence). The player is told. The infos of the phrase that asked are taken back: a dialog closed by its own info
-- (dont_has_info) would never offer the task again, to anybody. The engine carries the removal to the host and the others.
function _client_not_given(id, data)
	log("! the host could not give task '%s'", id)
	for _, info in ipairs(data.phrase_infos or {}) do
		if db.actor and db.actor:has_info(info) then
			db.actor:disable_info_portion(info)
			log("info '%s' of the phrase that asked for '%s' is taken back", info, id)
		end
	end
	local am = rawget(_G, "actor_menu")
	if type(am) == "table" and type(am.set_msg) == "function" then
		am.set_msg(1, game.translate_string("st_coop_news_task_not_given"), 8)
	end
end

local function client_apply_state(s)
	local rec = unpack_payload(s)
	local id = rec.i
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or is_local(id) then return end
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	stats.state_in = stats.state_in + 1
	if rec.d then
		local asked = stub_data(tm.task_info[id])
		local not_given = rec.r ~= nil and asked ~= nil and asked.pending_at ~= nil
		forget_task(tm, id)
		if not_given then
			local ok, err = pcall(_client_not_given, id, asked)
			if not ok then report("not given " .. id, err) end
		end
		return
	end
	cl.recv[id] = s
	local stub = tm.task_info[id]
	local data = stub_data(stub)
	if not data then
		stub, data = new_stub(id) -- also replaces a task object this machine loaded with the join save
		local ok, err = pcall(mirror_multifetch, id, true)
		if not ok then report("multifetch " .. id, err) end
	end
	local status = rec.s or "selected"
	local opt = data.optimistic
	if opt and status ~= "completed" and status ~= "fail" and now() - opt.at < PENDING_MS then
		status = data.status -- our turn-in is on its way: do not offer it again meanwhile
	else
		data.optimistic = nil
	end
	data.stage = rec.st or 0 -- a record built after an error has no stage, dialogs compare it
	data.status = status
	data.task_giver_id = rec.g and to_local_id(rec.g) or nil
	data.pending_at = nil
	tm.task_info[id] = stub
	if not rec.nv then apply_vars(id, type(rec.v) == "string" and unpack_payload(rec.v) or {}) end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(rec.bt) == "number" then b[id] = to_local_id(rec.bt) end
end

-- A part of the whole set (_f = number of the set, part _p of _n) or the keys that changed. "-key" = removed, "+key" = in the
-- set but too long to send. Only a whole set says what the host does not have: the last part drops the other keys.
local function client_apply_shared(payload)
	local vars = unpack_payload(payload)
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not ps then return end
	local gen = tonumber(vars._f)
	local full = cl.full
	if gen and not (full and full.gen == gen) then
		full = { gen = gen, got = 0, seen = {} }
		cl.full = full
	end
	if gen then full.got = full.got + 1 end
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		local mark = k:sub(1, 1)
		local key = (mark == "-" or mark == "+") and k:sub(2) or k
		if is_shared_key(key) then
			if mark == "-" then
				ps[key] = nil
			elseif mark ~= "+" then
				ps[key] = v
			end
			if gen and mark ~= "-" then full.seen[key] = true end
		end
	end
	if gen and vars._p == vars._n and full.got == vars._n then
		cl.full = nil
		local drop = {}
		for k in pairs(ps) do
			if is_shared_key(k) and not full.seen[k] then drop[#drop + 1] = k end
		end
		for _, k in ipairs(drop) do ps[k] = nil end
	end
end

-- save_var on this client's actor for a shared key: the host keeps the group's value.
local function client_route_var(k, v)
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	local old = ps and ps[k]
	local t = { k = k }
	if v == nil then
		t.op = "del"
	elseif type(v) == "number" and (old == nil or type(old) == "number") and k:sub(1, #COUNTER_PREFIX) == COUNTER_PREFIX then
		t.op, t.d = "add", v - (old or 0)
		if t.d == 0 then return end
	elseif var_value_ok(v) then
		t.op, t.v = "set", v
	else
		return
	end
	send(EV_VAR, pack(t, true), 0)
end

local function client_request_sync()
	cl.next_sync = now() + SYNC_RETRY_MS
	send(EV_SYNC, "", 0)
end

local function client_on_list(payload)
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local gen, part, parts, items = tostring(payload):match("^(%d+)/(%d+)/(%d+)|(.*)$")
	gen, part, parts = tonumber(gen), tonumber(part), tonumber(parts)
	if not (gen and part and parts) then return end
	local list = cl.list
	if not (list and list.gen == gen) then
		list = { gen = gen, got = 0, listed = {}, differ = false }
		cl.list = list
	end
	list.got = list.got + 1
	for item in items:gmatch("[^,]+") do
		local k, d = item:match("^([^:]*):(.*)$")
		if k then
			k = unesc(k)
			list.listed[k] = true
			local mine = cl.recv[k]
			if not mine or digest(mine) ~= d then list.differ = true end
		end
	end
	if part ~= parts or list.got ~= parts then return end -- a part went missing: this list says nothing
	cl.list = nil
	stats.lists = stats.lists + 1
	local listed, differ = list.listed, list.differ
	local drop = {}
	for id, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		if not listed[id] and not is_local(id) then
			local data = stub_data(tsk)
			if not (data and data.pending_at and now() - data.pending_at < PENDING_MS) then drop[#drop + 1] = id end
		end
	end
	for _, id in ipairs(drop) do forget_task(tm, id) end
	cl.synced = true
	if differ and now() >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
end

client_request = function(op, id, extra)
	if type(id) ~= "string" then return false end
	local t = extra or {}
	t.op, t.i = op, id
	local ok = send(EV_REQ, pack(t), 0)
	if ok then stats.req_out = stats.req_out + 1 end
	return ok
end

local function client_give(tm, id, giver)
	local gid = tonumber(giver)
	local extra = { g = gid and to_host_id(gid) or nil }
	local v = pack(task_vars(id), true)
	if #v > 9000 then
		log("! task vars of '%s' too long (%d characters), the host keeps its own", id, #v)
		v = ""
	end
	if v ~= "" then extra.v = v end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(b[id]) == "number" then extra.bt = to_host_id(b[id]) end
	if db.actor and db.actor:is_talking() and type(rawget(_G, "get_speaker")) == "function" then
		local ok, npc = pcall(get_speaker) -- whom this player talks to: the host's on_init of the task may ask for him
		local sid = ok and npc and npc.id and npc:id() or nil
		if type(sid) == "number" and sid ~= 0 then extra.sp = to_host_id(sid) end
	end
	if not client_request("give", id, extra) then return false end
	local stub, data = new_stub(id)
	data.task_giver_id = gid
	data.pending_at = now()
	if db.actor and db.actor:is_talking() then -- asked by a phrase: its infos go with the stub (client_on_info)
		data.phrase_infos = {}
		local a = cl.asking
		if not (a and a.at == now()) then
			a = { at = now(), stubs = {} }
			cl.asking = a
		end
		a.stubs[#a.stubs + 1] = data
	end
	tm.task_info[id] = stub
	cl.want_active = { id = id, at = now() }
	log("asked the host for task '%s'", id)
	return true
end

local function client_finish(tm, id, op)
	if not client_request(op, id) then return false end
	local data = stub_data(tm.task_info[id])
	if data and data.status ~= "completed" and data.status ~= "fail" then
		data.optimistic = { at = now(), status = data.status }
		data.status = op == "complete" and "completed" or "fail"
	end
	log("%s '%s' sent to the host", op, id)
	return true
end

-- The task this actor has as its active one (task_info holds every running task), id and engine task.
local function active_task(tm)
	local actor = db and db.actor
	if not actor then return nil end
	for id in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		local et = engine_task(id)
		if et then
			local ok, on = pcall(actor.is_active_task, actor, et)
			if ok and on == true then return id, et end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- A task this player took becomes his active one when the engine's copy arrives (a copy for somebody else's task leaves
-- it alone: coop_story apply_record). The host hears about the active task: the guide marker of a target on another level
-- is added by the host's task objects.
local function client_active_tick(tm, t)
	local want = cl.want_active
	if want then
		local et = engine_task(want.id)
		if et then
			pcall(db.actor.set_active_task, db.actor, et)
			cl.want_active = nil
		elseif t - want.at >= PENDING_MS then
			cl.want_active = nil
		end
	end
	local id = active_task(tm)
	if id ~= cl.active then
		if id then
			client_request("active", id)
		elseif cl.active then
			client_request("active", cl.active, { off = true })
		end
		cl.active = id
	end
end

local function client_tick()
	local t = now()
	if not cl.synced and t >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
	if t < cl.next_check then return end
	cl.next_check = t + 1000
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local ok, err = pcall(client_active_tick, tm, t)
	if not ok then report("active task", err) end
	local stale = false
	for _, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		local data = stub_data(tsk)
		if data then
			if data.pending_at and t - data.pending_at >= PENDING_MS then
				data.pending_at = nil
				stale = true
			end
			local opt = data.optimistic
			if opt and t - opt.at >= PENDING_MS then
				data.status = opt.status
				data.optimistic = nil
				stale = true
			end
		end
	end
	if stale and t >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
end

-- Host events for this player
local function apply_stat(t)
	local gs = rawget(_G, "game_statistics") or game_statistics
	if type(gs) ~= "table" then return end
	if t.f == "rank" then
		gs.increment_rank(tonumber(t.n) or 0)
	elseif t.f == "rept" then
		gs.increment_reputation(tonumber(t.n) or 0)
	elseif type(t.f) == "string" then
		gs.increment_statistic(t.f, tonumber(t.r), tonumber(t.p))
	end
end

local function client_on_reward(payload, from)
	if from ~= 0 or not is_client() then return end
	if not db.actor then
		cl.synced = false -- an effect in this event is sent again on the next sync
		return
	end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local q = type(t.q) == "number" and t.q or nil
	if q and cl.fx_done[q] then
		send(EV_ACK, tostring(q), 0)
		return
	end
	stats.rewards_in = stats.rewards_in + 1
	if t.k == "mn" and type(t.n) == "number" then
		-- the money itself is the host's (coop.money_grant, shown with the engine's balance): only the news line here
		local n = t.n >= 0 and math_floor(t.n) or -math_floor(-t.n)
		if n ~= 0 then news_manager.relocate_money(db.actor, n > 0 and "in" or "out", n > 0 and n or -n) end
	elseif t.k == "news" and type(t.s) == "string" then
		news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, t.ty == "out" and "out" or "in", t.s, tonumber(t.n) or 1)
	elseif t.k == "away" then
		-- what the group's rewards brought while this player was out of the game (coop_reward_group)
		local nw, rg = news_mod(), reward_group()
		if nw and nw.show_rewards and rg then
			nw.show_rewards(tonumber(t.c) or 0, tonumber(t.m) or 0, rg.parse_items(t.i), tonumber(t.x) or 0)
		end
	elseif t.k == "gw" and type(t.c) == "string" then
		local mlr = rawget(_G, "dialogs_mlr") or dialogs_mlr
		if mlr and mlr.show_goodwill_change_message then mlr.show_goodwill_change_message(t.c, nil, nil, t.g == true) end
	elseif t.k == "fx" and type(t.f) == "string" and FORWARD_EFFECTS[t.f] then
		local f = xr_effects and xr_effects[t.f]
		if type(f) == "function" then f(db.actor, nil, { t.p1, t.p2, t.p3, t.p4 }) end
	elseif t.k == "stat" then
		apply_stat(t)
	elseif t.k == "lang" then
		-- texts of tasks are final strings of the host's language: said once, at the first sync
		if type(t.l) == "string" and not cl.lang_told and game.translate_string("general_new_task") ~= t.l then
			cl.lang_told = true
			local nw = news_mod()
			if nw and nw.show_language then nw.show_language() end
		end
	end
	if q then
		cl.fx_done[q] = true
		send(EV_ACK, tostring(q), 0)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Messages of the shared journal (docs\MESSAGES.md)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The stock lines "New task" / "Task updated" / "Task completed" / "Task failed" / "Task reversed" are
-- news_manager.send_task. The host's scripts call it ("new" and "complete" from the actor's task callback the engine fires
-- for a state it sets itself, "fail" from task_manager.task_callback, "updated" / "reversed" from the task objects). On a
-- client the engine applies the host's copy of a task silently (a finished one without any callback) and fires the callback
-- for a new one once, so the client's own send_task is dropped for a group task and the host's call is sent to every
-- client instead, as event coop_tn: kind, task id, title, icon and the player who caused it. One line per event per
-- machine. The line the one who did it sees is the stock one; the others see "<nick> took a task" and so on
-- (coop_quests_news.show_task), the host included when a client did it.
local NEWS_KINDS = { new = true, updated = true, complete = true, fail = true, reversed = true }
local NEWS_NICK_KINDS = { new = true, complete = true, fail = true } -- updated / reversed: nobody did it
local NEWS_DEDUP_MS = { updated = 3000 }
local NEWS_DEDUP_DEFAULT_MS = 1500
local NEWS_LIMIT, NEWS_WINDOW_MS, NEWS_SEEN_MAX = 20, 10000, 200 -- lines a machine takes / sends in a window
local news_out_win = { at = 0, n = 0 }
local news_in_win = { at = 0, n = 0 }
local orig_send_task = nil -- news_manager.send_task as it was before the wrapper


local function nick_of(peer)
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == peer and type(p.nick) == "string" and p.nick ~= "" then return p.nick end
	end
	return "#" .. tostring(peer)
end

local function cut(s, n)
	s = type(s) == "string" and s or ""
	if #s > n then s = s:sub(1, n) end
	return s
end

local function window_ok(win)
	local t = now()
	if t - win.at >= NEWS_WINDOW_MS or t < win.at then win.at, win.n = t, 0 end
	if win.n >= NEWS_LIMIT then return false end
	win.n = win.n + 1
	return true
end

local function task_id_of(tsk)
	local ok, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
	if ok and type(id) == "string" and id ~= "" then return id end
	return nil
end

local function task_text(tsk)
	local title, icon
	pcall(function() title = tsk:get_title() end)
	pcall(function() icon = tsk:get_icon_name() end)
	return type(title) == "string" and title or "", (type(icon) == "string" and icon ~= "") and icon or nil
end

-- Host: the player whose action caused this event (a peer, 0 = the host), or nil: nobody (a script, a timer).
-- Second value: a "fail" the player asked for (cancel).
local function event_actor(kind, id)
	if kind == "new" then return host.given_by[id], false end
	if kind == "complete" then
		local by = ctx and ctx.task == id and ctx.by or nil
		if by == nil then by = host.finisher[id] end
		if by == nil then by = host.given_by[id] end -- a script completed it: the one who took it
		return by, false
	end
	if kind == "fail" then
		if ctx and ctx.task == id then return ctx.by, ctx.cancelled == true end
		local tm = tmgr()
		local rtask = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
		return host.finisher[id], is_task(rtask) and rtask.cancelled_by_actor == true
	end
	return nil, false
end

-- Host: the event to every client (deduped, limited). False if it was not sent.
local function news_out(kind, id, title, icon, by, cancelled, story)
	local key = kind .. " " .. id
	local t = now()
	local last = host.news_seen[key]
	if last and t >= last and t - last < (NEWS_DEDUP_MS[kind] or NEWS_DEDUP_DEFAULT_MS) then return false end
	if not window_ok(news_out_win) then
		stats.news_limited = stats.news_limited + 1
		return false
	end
	if host.news_count >= NEWS_SEEN_MAX then host.news_seen, host.news_count = {}, 0 end
	if host.news_seen[key] == nil then host.news_count = host.news_count + 1 end
	host.news_seen[key] = t
	local rec = { k = kind, i = id, ti = cut(title, 160), ic = icon and cut(icon, 100) or nil }
	if by ~= nil then
		rec.by = by
		rec.n = cut(nick_of(by), 32)
	end
	if cancelled then rec.c = true end
	if story then rec.sl = true end
	send(EV_NEWS, pack(rec), -1)
	stats.news_out = stats.news_out + 1
	return true
end

-- Host, a send_task call: the event to the clients; true if the host's own line was shown here (the nick variant for
-- a client's action), false to let the stock line follow.
local function host_news(kind, tsk)
	local id = task_id_of(tsk)
	if not id or is_local(id) then return false end
	local by, cancelled = event_actor(kind, id)
	local title, icon = task_text(tsk)
	news_out(kind, id, title, icon, by, cancelled, kind == "new" and task_is_story(id))
	if by ~= nil and by ~= 0 and NEWS_NICK_KINDS[kind] then
		local n = news_mod()
		if n and n.show_task then return n.show_task(kind, title, icon, nick_of(by), cancelled) == true end
	end
	return false
end

function news_actor(kind, id)
	if not is_host() or type(id) ~= "string" then return nil, false end
	return event_actor(kind, id)
end

local function wrap_send_task(orig)
	return function(actor, kind, tsk, ...)
		if NEWS_KINDS[kind] then
			if is_client() then
				local id = task_id_of(tsk)
				if id and not is_local(id) then
					stats.news_swallowed = stats.news_swallowed + 1
					return true -- the host's event carries the group's line
				end
			elseif is_host() and has_clients() then
				local ok, shown = pcall(host_news, kind, tsk)
				if not ok then
					report("task news", shown)
				elseif shown then
					return true
				end
			end
		end
		return orig(actor, kind, tsk, ...)
	end
end

-- Client: the stock line for a task the host announced (the stock function gets a stand-in for the engine task).
local function show_stock(kind, id, title, icon)
	local send_task = orig_send_task
	if not send_task then
		local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
		send_task = nm and nm.send_task
	end
	if type(send_task) ~= "function" then return end
	local stand_in = { id = id }
	function stand_in.get_id() return id end
	function stand_in.get_title() return title end
	function stand_in.get_icon_name() return icon end
	local ok, err = pcall(send_task, db.actor, kind, stand_in)
	if not ok then
		-- a mod's override of the stock function failed (e.g. in a dialog): the line is still shown
		report("task line " .. kind .. " " .. id, err)
		local n = news_mod()
		if n and n.show_plain then n.show_plain(kind, title, icon) end
	end
end

local function client_on_news(payload, from)
	if from ~= 0 or not client_live() or not db.actor then return end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local kind, id = t.k, t.i
	if not NEWS_KINDS[kind] or type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or #id > 128 or is_local(id) then return end
	if not window_ok(news_in_win) then
		stats.news_limited = stats.news_limited + 1
		return
	end
	stats.news_in = stats.news_in + 1
	local title = cut(t.ti, 160)
	local icon = (type(t.ic) == "string" and t.ic ~= "") and cut(t.ic, 100) or nil
	local by = tonumber(t.by)
	local n = news_mod()
	-- the storyline fade: the host's task object shows it in its constructor, a client has only stubs
	if t.sl == true and kind == "new" and n and n.show_story then n.show_story(title) end
	if by ~= nil and by ~= self_peer() and NEWS_NICK_KINDS[kind] then
		local nick = type(t.n) == "string" and t.n ~= "" and t.n or nick_of(by)
		if n and n.show_task and n.show_task(kind, title, icon, nick, t.c == true) then return end
	end
	show_stock(kind, id, title, icon)
end

local function patch_task_news()
	local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
	if not (nm and type(nm.send_task) == "function") then
		log("! news_manager.send_task not found: the group gets no task lines")
		return
	end
	orig_send_task = nm.send_task
	nm.send_task = wrap_send_task(orig_send_task)
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- task_manager patches (installed once; every wrapper checks the role when called)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local patched = false

-- Host: the player a task given by a script belongs to: the one nearest to its giver, or to the zone of the effect that gave
-- it. A task nothing locates stays the host's.
local function nearest_taker(giver)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if not (type(qc) == "table" and qc.nearest_character) then return 0 end
	local pos, gv
	local function place_of(o)
		local ok, p = pcall(function() return o:position() end)
		local ok2, v = pcall(function() return o:game_vertex_id() end)
		return ok and p or nil, ok2 and type(v) == "number" and v or nil
	end
	local near = host.give_near
	if near then pos, gv = place_of(near) end
	if not pos and type(giver) == "number" then
		local o = level.object_by_id(giver)
		if o then
			pos, gv = place_of(o)
		else
			local se = rawget(_G, "alife_object") and alife_object(giver)
			pos, gv = se and se.position or nil, se and se.m_game_vertex_id or nil
		end
	end
	-- A seat that plays no character: its ghost takes no task. With nobody to measure to (a script gave it with no giver:
	-- operacia_monolith's PDA in the group's inventory), or nobody on that level, a player of the world takes it, the one
	-- who has been in it longest (the lowest peer): rewards written on the ghost were nobody's.
	local function anybody()
		if not (qc.actor_is_nobody and qc.actor_is_nobody() and qc.bodies) then return 0 end
		local first
		for _, c in ipairs(qc.bodies()) do
			if type(c.peer) == "number" and c.peer ~= 0 and (not first or c.peer < first) then first = c.peer end
		end
		return first or 0
	end
	if not pos then return anybody() end
	-- Split levels: only a player of that level is next to it; the world server's own characters are not all there is, and the
	-- coordinates of two levels do not compare (the quest audit, 2026-11-13: a task given by logic was written on the ghost).
	local _, peer
	if qc.nearest_body then
		_, peer = qc.nearest_body({ position = pos, m_game_vertex_id = gv })
	else
		_, peer = qc.nearest_character(pos)
	end
	if not peer or peer == 0 then return anybody() end
	return peer
end

local function patch_method(name, make)
	local tm = tmgr()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local cls = mod and mod.CRandomTask
	if cls then
		local ok, f = pcall(function() return cls[name] end)
		if ok and type(f) == "function" then
			local w = make(f)
			local set_ok = pcall(function() cls[name] = w end)
			local read_ok, back = pcall(function() return cls[name] end)
			if set_ok and read_ok and back == w then return true end
		end
	end
	if tm then -- the class is not reachable: patch the manager object itself
		local ok, f = pcall(function() return tm[name] end)
		if ok and type(f) == "function" then
			local w = make(f)
			if pcall(function() tm[name] = w end) then return true end
		end
	end
	log("! task_manager:%s could not be patched", name)
	return false
end

local function patch_task_manager()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	if not mod then
		log("! task_manager not found: tasks are not shared in Lua")
		return
	end

	patch_method("give_task", function(orig)
		return function(self, id, giver, ...)
			if is_local(id) then return orig(self, id, giver, ...) end
			if is_client() then
				if not client_live() then return end -- loading the host's world: the host has it already
				local ok, res = pcall(client_give, self, id, giver)
				if ok and res then return end
				report("give " .. tostring(id), ok and "send failed" or res)
				return
			end
			if is_host() and type(id) == "string" then
				-- news: a player's action gave it (a request, the host's own dialog, the reward of a player's task)
				local who = host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id]
				if who == nil and ctx and ctx.rcpt ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 then who = ctx.rcpt end
				if who == nil and host_talking() then who = 0 end
				host.given_by[id] = who
				-- a follow-up task given by a reward belongs to the player who earned it
				host.taker[id] = host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id] or (ctx and ctx.rcpt) or 0
				if who == nil and ctx == nil and has_clients() then host.taker[id] = nearest_taker(giver) end
				host.taker_note[id] = nil
				host.finisher[id] = nil
				host.taker_char[id] = character_of(host.taker[id])
				host.participants[id] = reward_mode() >= EVERYONE_SHARED and participant_ids() or nil
				host.failure_participants[id] = participant_ids()
				host.rep_party[id] = participant_ids()
				-- the engine makes every new task the active one: a task another player took leaves the host's alone
				local keep = nil
				if host.taker[id] ~= 0 then keep = select(2, active_task(self)) end
				local prev_ctx = ctx
				if ctx == nil then
					-- W5: on_init (start items, PDAs) is the taker's, not a story reward for the whole group
					local t = host.taker[id]
					ctx = { task = id, rcpt = t, character = host.taker_char[id], share = false }
				end
				local res = { pcall(orig, self, id, giver, ...) }
				ctx = prev_ctx
				if keep then pcall(db.actor.set_active_task, db.actor, keep) end
				if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
				return unpack(res, 2)
			end
			return orig(self, id, giver, ...)
		end
	end)

	for name, op in pairs({ set_task_completed = "complete", set_task_failed = "fail", set_task_cancelled = "cancel" }) do
		patch_method(name, function(orig)
			return function(self, id, ...)
				if is_local(id) then return orig(self, id, ...) end
				if is_client() then
					if client_live() then
						local ok, err = pcall(client_finish, self, id, op)
						if not ok then report(name .. " " .. tostring(id), err) end
					end
					return
				end
				if is_host() and type(id) == "string" and host.finisher[id] == nil then
					-- a client's request, or the host turning it in in a dialog; a script completing it on
					-- its own leaves the reward to the player who took the task
					if host.exec_peer then
						host.finisher[id] = host.exec_peer
					elseif host_talking() then
						host.finisher[id] = 0
					end
				end
				return orig(self, id, ...)
			end
		end)
	end

	-- A client never evaluates the group's tasks: the host's scripts do, its state is mirrored here.
	-- Personal tasks are checked where they are.
	patch_method("update", function(orig)
		return function(self, ...)
			if is_client() then
				if next(local_tasks) and type(self.task_info) == "table" then
					for id, tsk in pairs(self.task_info) do
						if is_local(id) and not stub_data(tsk) and type(tsk.check_task) == "function" then
							local ok, err = pcall(tsk.check_task, tsk, self)
							if not ok then report("local task " .. id, err) end
						end
					end
				end
				return
			end
			return orig(self, ...)
		end
	end)
	for _, name in ipairs({ "task_complete", "task_fail" }) do
		patch_method(name, function(orig)
			return function(self, id, ...)
				if is_client() and not is_local(id) then return false end
				return orig(self, id, ...)
			end
		end)
		local f = mod[name]
		if type(f) == "function" then
			mod[name] = function(id, ...)
				if is_client() and not is_local(id) then return false end
				return f(id, ...)
			end
		end
	end

	local cb = mod.task_callback
	if type(cb) == "function" then
		mod.task_callback = function(tsk, state)
			if is_client() then
				local ok, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
				if ok and is_local(id) then return cb(tsk, state) end
				return -- results come from the host (silently, see coop_story)
			end
			if is_host() then return host_task_callback(cb, tsk, state) end
			return cb(tsk, state)
		end
	end
end

-- Guide markers (a target on another level): the host's task objects add them for the host's active task only. The same
-- check runs for each client's active task, and the marker of a target somebody still needs stays when the host's own target
-- is on this level. The markers are the group's, a client sees those of the others too. A player on a map server's level has
-- his on the exits of his level: the check looks from there (far view); the stock spot goes to him through coop_story.
local function target_elsewhere(target)
	local ok, yes = pcall(function()
		local se = alife_object(target)
		if not se then return false end
		return alife():level_name(game_graph():vertex(se.m_game_vertex_id):level_id()) ~= level.name()
	end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function guide_wanted()
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not (tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table") then return false end
	for _, id in pairs(host.active) do
		local rt = tm.task_info[id]
		if is_task(rt) and rt.current_target ~= nil and target_elsewhere(rt.current_target) then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function host_guides()
	local tm = tmgr()
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if not (next(host.active) and tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" and type(qc) == "table" and qc.with_actor) then return end
	local fields = { is_active_task = function() return true end }
	for peer, id in pairs(host.active) do
		local rt = tm.task_info[id]
		local body = avatar_obj(peer)
		if not peer_in_session(peer) then
			host.active[peer] = nil -- left the game
		elseif body and is_task(rt) and rt.check_level and rt.current_target ~= nil then
			local ok, err = true, nil
			if body.far then
				ok, err = qc.with_level_of(peer, qc.with_actor, fields, rt.check_level, rt, rt.current_target)
			elseif target_elsewhere(rt.current_target) then
				ok, err = qc.with_actor(fields, rt.check_level, rt, rt.current_target)
			end
			if not ok then report("guide of #" .. tostring(peer), err) end
		end
	end
end

local function patch_guides()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_objects") or task_objects
	local cls = mod and mod.CGeneralTask
	local orig = cls and cls.remove_guider_spot
	if type(orig) ~= "function" then return end
	cls.remove_guider_spot = function(self, ...)
		if is_host() and guide_wanted() then return end
		return orig(self, ...)
	end
end

local function patch_shared_vars()
	local orig = rawget(_G, "save_var")
	if type(orig) ~= "function" then
		log("! save_var not found: shared task vars written on a client stay local")
		return
	end
	_G.save_var = function(obj, k, v)
		if client_live() and is_shared_key(k) and is_my_actor(obj) then
			local ok, err = pcall(client_route_var, k, v)
			if not ok then report("shared var " .. tostring(k), err) end
		end
		return orig(obj, k, v)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Update, events, start
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local next_tick = 0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: worlds hurt by a give that died
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Split levels, builds 45-49: a task whose on_init makes a squad next to the player died on the world server (the far view handed
-- the stock smart terrain a stand-in of the new squad, coop_quests_far object_there). The dialog phrase had given its info already
-- and the dialog is closed by it (dont_has_info): the task can be asked for by nobody. `info` is taken back when the task is not
-- on and none of the infos its own run sets (`ran`) is here. Once a world: a task dropped later is the player's choice.
host.lost_gives = {
	{ info = "fanat_training_start_done", task = "task_fanat_training_1",
		ran = { "fanat_training_boars_death_done", "fanat_training_back_to_village_done", "esc_2_12_stalker_fanat_death" } },
	{ info = "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_start", task = "cs_task0_ambush_renegade_story",
		ran = { "renegade_cs_story_squad_1_death", "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_done" } },
	{ info = "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_done", task = "cs_task0_ambush_renegade_story2",
		ran = { "renegade_cs_story_squad_2_death", "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_done2" } },
	{ info = "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_done2", task = "cs_task0_ambush_renegade_story3",
		ran = { "renegade_cs_story_squad_3_death", "cs_story_task0_ambush_renegade_done3" } },
}

function heal_lost_gives()
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not (tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" and db.actor) then return 0 end
	local healed = 0
	for _, e in ipairs(host.lost_gives) do
		-- the give that died left the task object in the journal with no task of the engine behind it: lost all the same
		local half = tm.task_info[e.task] ~= nil and not engine_task_running(e.task)
		local lost = has_alife_info(e.info) and task_known(e.task) and (tm.task_info[e.task] == nil or half)
		for _, info in ipairs(e.ran) do lost = lost and not has_alife_info(info) end
		if lost then
			if half then tm.task_info[e.task] = nil end
			db.actor:disable_info_portion(e.info)
			healed = healed + 1
			log("task '%s' was asked for and never given: info '%s' is taken back, its dialog offers it again", e.task, e.info)
		end
	end
	return healed
end

function _heal_once()
	local l = api.levels
	if not (l and l.split and l.split()) or not db.actor then return end
	if load_var(db.actor, "coop_lost_gives", false) then return end
	save_var(db.actor, "coop_lost_gives", true)
	local ok, err = pcall(heal_lost_gives)
	if not ok then report("lost gives", err) end
end

local function actor_on_update()
	if not api then return end
	local t = now()
	if api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server() == true and t >= host.map_retry then
		host.map_retry = t + 1000
		for _, wait in pairs(host.fx_wait) do
			for _, e in ipairs(wait) do send("coop_rep_map", e.s, 0) end
		end
	end
	if t < next_tick then return end
	next_tick = t + 250
	if is_host() and next(host.fines) ~= nil then flush_fines() end
	if is_host() then
		if not host.healed then
			host.healed = true
			_heal_once()
		end
		if not has_clients() then return end
		if t >= host.next_scan then
			host.next_scan = t + SCAN_MS
			host_scan(false)
			host_guides()
		end
		if t >= host.next_list then
			host.next_list = t + LIST_MS
			host_list(-1)
		end
	elseif client_live() then
		client_tick()
	end
end

-- level.add_call runs every frame of the level. Stock actor_binder:update returns while the actor is dead, before
-- task_manager:update and before the actor_on_update callback: the host's revive delay, longer for a wipe, would stop the
-- group's tasks, their mirror and every client's turn-in (the stub falls back to open after PENDING_MS). A live actor's
-- binder does all of this itself.
local function actor_dead()
	local a = db and db.actor
	if not a then return false end
	local ok, alive = pcall(a.alive, a)
	return ok and alive == false
end

local function dead_tick()
	if not (api and active() and actor_dead()) then return false end
	local t = now()
	if is_host() and t >= host.next_dead_update then
		host.next_dead_update = t + DEAD_UPDATE_MS
		local tm = tmgr()
		if tm then
			local ok, err = pcall(tm.update, tm)
			if not ok then report("task update while dead", err) end
		end
	end
	local ok, err = pcall(actor_on_update) -- the host runs a unique call without a guard
	if not ok then report("tick while dead", err) end
	return false
end

local function actor_on_reinit()
	if type(AddUniqueCall) == "function" then AddUniqueCall(dead_tick) end
end

local function guarded(what, f)
	return function(...)
		local ok, err = pcall(f, ...)
		if not ok then report(what, err) end
	end
end

local function register_events()
	local cm = rawget(_G, "coop_main") or coop_main
	if not (cm and cm.add_event_handler) then
		log("! coop_main.add_event_handler not found: task events are not handled")
		return
	end
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_REQ, guarded("task request", host_on_request))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_SYNC, guarded("task sync", function(_, from)
		if is_host() and type(from) == "number" and from ~= 0 then
			host_full_sync(from)
			local rg = reward_group()
			local id = rg and rg.id_of(from)
			if id then host.char_of[from] = id end
			local e = id and rg.take(id)
			if e then send_reward(from, { k = "away", m = e.m, c = e.c, x = e.x, i = rg.items_text(e.i) }) end
			host_resend_effects(from)
			send_reward(from, { k = "lang", l = game.translate_string("general_new_task") })
		end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_STATE, guarded("task state", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and is_client() then client_apply_state(payload) end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_LIST, guarded("task list", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and is_client() then client_on_list(payload) end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_REWARD, guarded("task reward", client_on_reward))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_NEWS, guarded("task news", client_on_news))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_VAR, guarded("shared var", host_on_var))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_ACK, guarded("effect answer", host_on_effect_ack))
	cm.add_event_handler("coop_rep_map_ack", guarded("map effect answer", function(payload, from)
		if from ~= 0 or not (api.is_map_server and api.is_map_server() == true) then return end
		local q = tonumber(payload)
		for _, wait in pairs(host.fx_wait) do
			for i, e in ipairs(wait) do if e.q == q then table.remove(wait, i); return end end
		end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler("coop_rep_map", guarded("map personal effect", function(payload, from)
		if not is_host() or type(from) ~= "number" or from < 0x100 then return end
		local effect = unpack_payload(payload)
		if (effect.k ~= "stat" and not (effect.k == "fx" and FORWARD_EFFECTS[effect.f]))
			or type(effect.f) ~= "string" or #effect.f > 80
			or type(effect.e) ~= "string" or #effect.e > 100 or type(effect.q) ~= "number" or effect.q < 1 or effect.q % 1 ~= 0
			or type(effect.i) ~= "number" then return end
		-- character 0 is the host player's; a world server whose seat plays no character has only its ghost there (owner 2026-11-13)
		local member = effect.i == 0 and not (api.is_dedicated and api.is_dedicated() == true)
		for _, p in ipairs(players()) do if p.avatar_id == effect.i then member = true end end
		local group = reward_group()
		for _, m in ipairs(group and group.list() or {}) do if m.id == effect.i then member = true end end
		if not member then return end
		local q = effect.q
		local key = tostring(from) .. ":" .. effect.e .. ":" .. tostring(q)
		if not host.map_seen[key] then
			with_character(effect.i, function()
				if effect.i == 0 then
					if effect.k == "stat" then apply_stat(effect)
					else xr_effects[effect.f](db.actor, nil, {effect.p1, effect.p2, effect.p3, effect.p4}) end
				else effect.q, effect.e, effect.i = nil, nil, nil; send_effect(ctx.rcpt, effect) end
			end)
			host.map_seen[key] = true
		end
		send("coop_rep_map_ack", tostring(q), from)
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_VARS, guarded("shared vars", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and is_client() then client_apply_shared(payload) end
	end))
end

-- Host: effects nobody answered yet, in the save: a restart of the host must not lose what was already paid for.
function save_effects(m_data)
	if is_client() then m_data.coop_task_fx_done = cl.fx_done; return end
	local wait
	for key, list in pairs(host.fx_wait) do
		if #list > 0 then
			wait = wait or {}
			wait[key] = list
		end
	end
	m_data.coop_task_fx = { seq = host.fx_seq, wait = wait, characters = host.char_of,
		takers = host.taker, taker_char = host.taker_char, participants = host.participants, rep_party = host.rep_party,
		failure_participants = host.failure_participants, map_seen = host.map_seen, fines = host.fines }
end

function load_effects(m_data)
	if is_client() then cl.fx_done = m_data.coop_task_fx_done or {}; return end
	local saved = m_data.coop_task_fx
	host.fx_seq = saved and saved.seq or 0
	host.fx_wait = saved and saved.wait or {}
	host.char_of = saved and saved.characters or {}
	host.taker = saved and saved.takers or {}
	host.taker_char = saved and saved.taker_char or {}
	host.participants = saved and saved.participants or {}
	host.rep_party = saved and saved.rep_party or {}
	host.failure_participants = saved and saved.failure_participants or {}
	host.map_seen = saved and saved.map_seen or {}
	host.fines = saved and saved.fines or {}
	m_data.coop_task_fx = nil
end

function print_status()
	local role = not api and "no engine API" or is_host() and "host" or is_client() and "client" or "off"
	local n_stub, n_real = 0, 0
	local tm = tmgr()
	if tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" then
		for _, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
			if stub_data(tsk) then n_stub = n_stub + 1 else n_real = n_real + 1 end
		end
	end
	log("role %s, tasks: %d script, %d mirrored | requests out %d in %d refused %d | states out %d in %d, lists %d, syncs %d",
		role, n_real, n_stub, stats.req_out, stats.req_in, stats.refused, stats.state_out, stats.state_in, stats.lists, stats.syncs)
	log("rewards routed %d received %d, share %s | group items: moved %d released %d, stages %d | errors %d",
		stats.rewards_routed, stats.rewards_in, tostring(reward_mode()), stats.party_moves, stats.party_releases,
		stats.stage_by_party, stats.errors)
	log("task lines: sent %d, received %d, own engine lines dropped %d, limited %d", stats.news_out, stats.news_in,
		stats.news_swallowed, stats.news_limited)
	if is_host() then
		for id, peer in pairs(host.taker) do
			if peer ~= 0 and tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id] then log("  '%s' taken by #%s", id, tostring(peer)) end
		end
	end
	-- the rest of the quests group (offers, group items, story, PDA)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if type(qc) == "table" and type(qc.print_status) == "function" then
		local ok, err = pcall(qc.print_status)
		if not ok then report("quests status", err) end
	end
end

function on_game_start()
	if not api then return end
	local md = _G.coop_economy_mdata
	if md and md.register_player_key then md.register_player_key("coop_task_fx_done", function() return cl.fx_done end) end
	if not patched then
		patched = true
		local steps = {
			{ "task_manager", patch_task_manager },
			{ "task news", patch_task_news },
			{ "rewards", patch_rewards },
			{ "statistics", patch_statistics },
			{ "stash lines", patch_stash_line },
			{ "guide markers", patch_guides },
			{ "group items", patch_party_items },
			{ "shared vars", patch_shared_vars },
			{ "events", register_events },
		}
		for _, s in ipairs(steps) do
			local ok, err = pcall(s[2])
			if not ok then report("install " .. s[1], err) end
		end
		if api.party_has == nil then
			pcall(function()
				api.party_has = party_has
				api.party_count = party_count
			end)
		end
	end
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_update", actor_on_update)
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_reinit", actor_on_reinit)
	RegisterScriptCallback("save_state", save_effects)
	RegisterScriptCallback("load_state", load_effects)
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_info_callback", _client_on_info)
	-- Parity audit D10: this machine dropped events (a long stall): one of them may be a task's, ask for the whole list
	RegisterScriptCallback("coop_events_lost", function()
		if client_live() then client_request_sync() end
	end)
	-- The host's move: this player stayed in his world, the world server's Lua is new: who he is, what task he has on is told again
	RegisterScriptCallback("coop_world_back", function()
		if client_live() then
			cl.active = nil
			client_request_sync()
		end
	end)
end
